es/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/f2-gaps.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F2 compact: with missing: 'zero' on the field, an explicit null and an absent step are drawn at zero, on the zero baseline\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"gaps\": {\n      \"line\": \"An absent step on a regular time (instant) axis is tested only at the data stage (test/data/review.test.ts, where it becomes a gap slot with AX105); no chart test draws one. Every drawn absent-step test uses a date axis.\",\n      \"area\": \"An absent step on a regular time (instant) axis is tested only at the data stage (test/data/review.test.ts, where it becomes a gap slot with AX105); no chart test draws one. Every drawn absent-step test uses a date axis.\",\n      \"bar\": \"An absent step on a regular time (instant) axis is tested only at the data stage (test/data/review.test.ts, where it becomes a gap slot with AX105); no chart test draws one. Every drawn absent-step test uses a date axis.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"No test asserts that an explicit null on a scatter raises no diagnostic.\",\n      \"donut\": \"No test reads the tooltip of a null slice (it has no arc, so it can be reached only by keyboard).\",\n      \"compact\": \"Only the compact line is drawn in Chrome (gaps, the isolated point, the absent-step gap, missing: 'zero'); for compact area and bar, including the bar's \\\"no data\\\" mark, the evidence is the Node scene. The property over generated missing indexes runs on compact area only. An absent step on a regular time (instant) axis is tested only at the data stage (test/data/review.test.ts, where it becomes a gap slot with AX105); no chart test draws one. Every drawn absent-step test uses a date axis.\"\n    },\n    \"limits\": {\n      \"line\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Gaps are read from the SVG path's vertices and from screenshots with the gridlines made transparent; the readouts from the tooltip's text, the table's accessibility tree and the plot's value text.\",\n      \"area\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Gaps are read from the SVG path's vertices and from screenshots with the gridlines made transparent; the readouts from the tooltip's text, the table's accessibility tree and the plot's value text.\",\n      \"bar\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. The \\\"no data\\\" mark is checked painted for an explicit null on a category axis; at an absent date step and for an absent field it is checked in the Node scene. The readouts are read from the tooltip's text, the table's accessibility tree and the plot's value text.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. A point without a y has no position: the tests check that it is not drawn and that the keyboard skips it, so only the table can say \\\"No data\\\". Scatter draws no lines, so bridging, isolated points and absent steps do not reach it.\",\n      \"donut\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. The keyboard reading of null and absent slices is checked in Node; Chrome checks the arcs and the table.\",\n      \"compact\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. The Node tests run compact line, area and bar; a compact chart has no tooltip, table or keyboard reading, so the \\\"No data\\\" readouts do not reach it.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"F3\",\n    \"statement\": \"Input that cannot be plotted as given is reported, never guessed. The registry in section 3.5 fixes each code's level, delivery, what is drawn and what the reader sees: errors and warnings print once per code per page in every build, hints in development 