SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. The changed-values tests in Chrome replace the note's text through messages, so the default wording of that note is checked on the Node model only. The count-of-one case is checked in the development build.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. The changed-values tests in Chrome replace the note's text through messages, so the default wording of that note is checked on the Node model only. The count-of-one case is checked in the development build.\",\n      \"donut\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. The changed-values tests in Chrome replace the note's text through messages, so the default wording of that note is checked on the Node model only. The count-of-one case is checked in the development build.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"F10\",\n    \"statement\": \"Stacks place positive and negative values on their own sides of zero, and the axis covers both totals. The readout's total is the sum when every component has the same sign; with mixed signs it gives the positive total and the negative total, not their net. A missing component is drawn with zero height and the stack is marked \\\"incomplete\\\" in tooltip, table and announcements.\",\n    \"appliesTo\": [\n      \"area\",\n      \"bar\",\n      \"compact\"\n    ],\n    \"notApplicable\": {\n      \"line\": \"Line has no stacked variant.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"Scatter has no stacked variant.\",\n      \"donut\": \"A donut has slices, not stacks.\"\n    },\n    \"evidence\": {\n      \"area\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"property\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-stacks.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F10 area: for any generated mixed-sign area stacks each drawn component uses its own side of zero and the axis covers both sums\",\n          \"registration\": \"F10 ${type}: for any generated mixed-sign ${kind} stacks each drawn component uses its own side of zero and the axis covers both sums\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-stacks.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F10 area: a missing area component has zero height and the reader is told which stack is incomplete\",\n          \"registration\": \"F10 ${type}: a missing ${kind} component has zero height and the reader is told which stack is incomplete${type === 'compact' ? ' (reading: the summary provides the incomplete warning)' : ''}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/type-matrix.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-tooltip-area area: lists visible series in order and distinguishes No observation from No data\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F10 area: a stack with a positive and a negative part reads the positive total and the negative total in the tooltip, never their net, and the parts sit on their own sides of zero\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-tooltip-area: every visible series at that x and, stacked, the stack total, in series order; a hidden series is not listed\",\n          \"registration\": \"T-tooltip-${type}: every visible series at that ${type === 'bar' ? 'category' : 'x'}${type === 'area' ? ' and, stacked, the stack total' : ''}, in series order; a hidden series is not listed\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"bar\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"property\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-stacks.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F10 bar: for any generated mixed-sign bar stacks each drawn component uses its own side of zero and the axis covers both sums\",\n          \"registration\": \"F10 ${type}: for any generated mixed-sign ${kind} stacks each drawn component uses its own side of zero and the axis covers both sums\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-stacks.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F10 bar: a missing bar component has zero height and the reader is told which stack is incomplete\",\n          \"registration\": \"F10 ${type}: a missing ${kind} component has zero height and the reader is told which stack is incomplete${type === 'compact' ? ' (reading: the summary provides the incomplete warning)' : ''}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F10 bar: a stack with a positive and a negative part reads the positive total and the negative total in the tooltip, never their net, and the parts sit on their own sides of zero\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/lookup/aligned.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"uses the author’s mixed total format and leaves same-sign and all-zero totals plain\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"compact\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"property\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-stacks.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F10 compact: for any generated mixed-sign area stacks each drawn component uses its own side of zero and the axis covers both sums\",\n          \"registration\": \"F10 ${type}: for any generated mixed-sign ${kind} stacks each drawn component uses its own side of zero and the axis covers both sums\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"property\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-stacks.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F10 compact: for any generated mixed-sign bar stacks each drawn component uses its own side of zero and the axis covers both sums\",\n          \"registration\": \"F10 ${type}: for any generated mixed-sign ${kind} stacks each drawn component uses its own side of zero and the axis covers both sums\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-stacks.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F10 compact: a missing area component has zero height and the reader is told which stack is incomplete (reading: the summary provides the incomplete warning)\",\n          \"registration\": \"F10 ${type}: a missing ${kind} component has zero height and the reader is told which stack is incomplete${type === 'compact' ? ' (reading: the summary provides the incomplete warning)' : ''}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-stacks.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F10 compact: a missing bar component has zero height and the reader is told which stack is incomplete (reading: the summary provides the incomplete warning)\",\n          \"registration\": \"F10 ${type}: a missing ${kind} component has zero height and the reader is told which stack is incomplete${type === 'compact' ? ' (reading: the summary provides the incomplete warning)' : ''}\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"gaps\": {\n      \"bar\": \"No test checks that a stacked bar's tooltip marks an incomplete stack; the table row and the value text are checked.\"\n    },\n    \"limits\": {\n      \"area\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Sides of zero and the axis extent are asserted on the drawn scene (a property test over 1,000 generated stacks); painted sides are checked for bars only. \\\"Incomplete\\\" is asserted on the tooltip, table and value-text models, not on rendered text; the same-sign total is read in Chrome's tooltip.\",\n      \"bar\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Sides of zero and the axis extent are asserted on the drawn scene (a property test over 1,000 generated stacks) and, for one mixed-sign fixture, on painted bars. The same-sign total is checked on the lookup module (unit test).\",\n      \"compact\": \"Compact kinds run: area and bar (a line has no stacks). A compact chart has no tooltip, table or announcements, so the incomplete stack is checked in its description (the generated summary), as the cited test reads the spec. Geometry is asserted on the drawn scene.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"F8\",\n    \"statement\": \"Donut slices keep the given order, start at 12 o'clock and run clockwise; the legend shows every slice's value and percentage as text, in slice order. A zero slice is listed without an arc, a null slice as \\\"No data\\\". A negative value is AX120 and the chart shows its error state. With more than eight slices that have an arc, the seven largest are drawn and the rest of those are grouped as \\\"Other (n)\\\", with AX121; zero and null slices never count toward the limit and are never grouped; the table lists every category. Shares have at most one fraction digit. An all-zero donut shows the empty state.\",\n    \"appliesTo\": [\n      \"donut\"\n    ],\n    \"notApplicable\": {\n      \"line\": \"This slice rule is specific to donut.\",\n      \"area\": \"This slice rule is specific to donut.\",\n      \"bar\": \"This slice rule is specific to donut.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"This slice rule is specific to donut.\",\n      \"compact\": \"This slice rule is specific to donut.\"\n    },\n    \"evidence\": {\n      \"donut\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/f8-donut.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F8 donut: slices keep the given (unsorted) order, start at 12 o'clock and run clockwise: the ring at each slice's middle angle shows that slice's legend colour\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/f8-donut.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F8 donut: the legend shows every slice's value and percentage as text, in slice order, and is in the accessibility tree\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/f8-donut.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F8 donut: a zero slice is listed without an arc; a null slice is listed as \\\"No data\\\", without an arc\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/f8-donut.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F8 donut: a negative value is AX120 and the chart shows its error state inside the plot, with no slices\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/f8-donut.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F8 donut: ten slices in scrambled order draw the seven largest, in their given order, then \\\"Other (3)\\\" holding the other three, with AX121; arcs and legend agree; the table lists all ten in the given order\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/f8-donut.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F8 donut: eight slices are all drawn and raise no AX121; the ninth is what groups\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/f8-donut.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F8 donut: zero and null slices do not count toward the eight-slice limit and are never grouped: eight drawn slices plus a zero and a null raise no AX121 and list all ten, the zero and the null by name\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/f8-donut.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F8 donut: an all-zero donut shows the empty state inside the plot, with its exact message and no slices\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-dense-donut: no simplified drawing: eight slices, the smallest under 0.2 %, are each drawn at their angle in their colour\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/interaction.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"a donut with more than eight slices lists \\\"Other\\\" with its count, and a zero slice without an arc\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-donut.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F8 donut: slices start at twelve and run clockwise in input order; zero and null are listed without arcs\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-donut.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F8 donut: seven largest categories and Other (3) are drawn; all ten categories remain individually readable in the table\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-donut.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F8 donut: a negative value shows the error state and clears all arcs\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-donut.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F8 donut: all-zero values show the empty state while the table retains both zero values\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-donut.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F8 donut: exactly eight slices including zero and null keep both arcless categories readable\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-donut.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F8 donut: zero and null slices stay separate and only positive slices count toward the limit\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-format.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F6 donut: percentage text is independently localized in tooltip and table\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/format/index.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"a share of 5/29 reads 17.2%, in each locale\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/format/index.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"rounds the share as the decimal it is: 0.1235 is 12.4%, 1/3 is 33.3%\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"gaps\": {\n      \"donut\": \"No test groups slices while a null slice is present: that a null slice is never grouped is checked only without grouping; a zero slice is checked to stay on its own when grouping happens.\"\n    },\n    \"limits\": {\n      \"donut\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Shares in the rendered legend are whole percentages; the one-fraction-digit rounding is checked on the share formatter (unit tests) and on the Node tooltip, table and value-text models (12.5 %).\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"F4\",\n    \"statement\": \"Three temporal types, never mixed silently: calendar dates read the same in every viewer time zone; instants (epoch milliseconds declared time, Date objects, ISO strings with an offset) are shown in timeZone (default the viewer's), with the zone named in the tooltip heading and the description; wall-clock times are shown as written, with AX112; instants all on one time of day, whole days apart, raise AX111; a bare number is never taken for an instant.\",\n    \"appliesTo\": [\n      \"line\",\n      \"area\",\n      \"bar\",\n      \"scatter\",\n      \"compact\"\n    ],\n    \"notApplicable\": {\n      \"donut\": \"A donut has category labels and no temporal axis.\"\n    },\n    \"evidence\": {\n      \"line\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-time.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F4 line: calendar days, months and years keep their input precision across time zones (reading: month and year inputs keep their granularity)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-time.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F4 line: ISO with offset read in three local times, name the zone and raise AX111 for whole days (reading: Intl zone aliases name the same zone)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-time.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F4 line: Date objects read in three local times, name the zone and raise AX111 for whole days (reading: Intl zone aliases name the same zone)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-time.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F4 line: declared epoch milliseconds read in three local times, name the zone and raise AX111 for whole days (reading: Intl zone aliases name the same zone)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-time.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F4 line: declaring an instant column as date keeps its UTC calendar dates in every zone\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-time.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F4 line: DST spring skips an hour and fall repeats it with distinct zone abbreviations\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-time.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F4 line: wall-clock input stays as written through a DST transition and raises AX112\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-time.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F4 line: an impossible date is omitted, and bare epoch-like numbers remain numbers\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-time.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F4 line: mixing calendar dates with a wall time and an instant reports both incompatible rows (reading: a clear majority fixes the axis type)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a1-names.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A1 line: the summary of instants states the time zone they are shown in\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"property\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-time.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F4 line: generated instants around DST and the year boundary preserve elapsed time and local readouts\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/data.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"the dates fixture as date strings gives identical tick text in UTC, America/Los_Angeles and Asia/Kolkata\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"area\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-time.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F4 area: calendar days, months and years keep their input precision across time zones (reading: month and year inputs keep their granularity)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-time.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F4 area: ISO with offset read in three local time