ixing calendar dates with a wall time and an instant reports both incompatible rows (reading: a clear majority fixes the axis type)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a1-names.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A1 compact: the summary of instants states the time zone they are shown in\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"limits\": {\n      \"line\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Node evidence: the viewer's zone is set by the test host (UTC, America/Los_Angeles, Asia/Kolkata), and the tooltip heading, table and keyboard texts are read from the models the DOM shows. In Chrome, calendar-date tick text is compared in three real viewer zones, and the description of instants names the author's zone (Asia/Kolkata).\",\n      \"area\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Node evidence: the viewer's zone is set by the test host (UTC, America/Los_Angeles, Asia/Kolkata), and the tooltip heading, table and keyboard texts are read from the models the DOM shows. In Chrome only the description of instants is read, with the author's zone (Asia/Kolkata).\",\n      \"bar\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Node evidence: the viewer's zone is set by the test host (UTC, America/Los_Angeles, Asia/Kolkata), and the tooltip heading, table and keyboard texts are read from the models the DOM shows. In Chrome only the description of instants is read, with the author's zone (Asia/Kolkata).\",\n      \"scatter\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Node evidence: the viewer's zone is set by the test host (UTC, America/Los_Angeles, Asia/Kolkata), and the tooltip heading, table and keyboard texts are read from the models the DOM shows. In Chrome only the description of instants is read, with the author's zone (Asia/Kolkata).\",\n      \"compact\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. The Node tests run compact line, area and bar, with the viewer's zone set by the test host; a compact chart has no tooltip or table, so the zone and the dates are checked in its description. In Chrome a compact line's description of instants is read, with the author's zone (Asia/Kolkata).\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"F11\",\n    \"statement\": \"Line, area and scatter are drawn in x order whatever the input order; on line, area and bar two rows with the same x in one series are AX108 and that series is not drawn; on scatter, points sharing an x (or both coordinates) are ordinary data.\",\n    \"appliesTo\": [\n      \"line\",\n      \"area\",\n      \"bar\",\n      \"scatter\",\n      \"compact\"\n    ],\n    \"notApplicable\": {\n      \"donut\": \"A donut has slice labels, not an x axis; duplicate labels are AX108 under F3.\"\n    },\n    \"evidence\": {\n      \"line\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-order.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F11 line: shuffled observations draw in ascending x and the last value belongs to the largest x\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-order.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F11 line: duplicate x disables just the affected line series and the model identifies that series\",\n          \"registration\": \"F11 ${type}: duplicate x disables just the affected ${kind} series and the model identifies that series\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"area\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-order.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F11 area: shuffled observations draw in ascending x and the last value belongs to the largest x\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-order.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F11 area: duplicate x disables just the affected area series and the model identifies that series\",\n          \"registration\": \"F11 ${type}: duplicate x disables just the affected ${kind} series and the model identifies that series\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"bar\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-order.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F11 bar: duplicate x disables just the affected bar series and the model identifies that series\",\n          \"registration\": \"F11 ${type}: duplicate x disables just the affected ${kind} series and the model identifies that series\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"scatter\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-order.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F11 scatter: shuffled observations draw in ascending x and the last value belongs to the largest x\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-order.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F11 scatter: equal x and coincident coordinates are all drawn, with x then y order and original row provenance\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"property\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-order.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F11 scatter: generated unsorted and duplicate rows keep their x, y and caller row order\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"compact\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-order.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F11 compact: shuffled observations draw in ascending x and the last value belongs to the largest x\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-order.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F11 compact: duplicate x disables just the affected line series and the model identifies that series\",\n          \"registration\": \"F11 ${type}: duplicate x disables just the affected ${kind} series and the model identifies that series\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-order.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F11 compact: duplicate x disables just the affected area series and the model identifies that series\",\n          \"registration\": \"F11 ${type}: duplicate x disables just the affected ${kind} series and the model identifies that series\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-order.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F11 compact: duplicate x disables just the affected bar series and the model identifies that series\",\n          \"registration\": \"F11 ${type}: duplicate x disables just the affected ${kind} series and the model identifies that series\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/compact.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"C2 compact line: shuffled input draws the same marks as sorted input (F11), and the dirty fixture yields AX102, AX103 and AX106 (F3)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/compact.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"C2 compact area: shuffled input draws the same marks as sorted input (F11), and the dirty fixture yields AX102, AX103 and AX106 (F3)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/compact.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"C2 compact bar: shuffled input draws the same marks as sorted input (F11), and the dirty fixture yields AX102, AX103 and AX106 (F3)\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"limits\": {\n      \"line\": \"Node evidence: the scene the controller hands to the renderer, from a three-point shuffled fixture (not the trend fixture), plus the table and keyboard order.\",\n      \"area\": \"Node evidence: the scene the controller hands to the renderer, from a three-point shuffled fixture (not the trend fixture), plus the table and keyboard order.\",\n      \"bar\": \"Node evidence: the scene and the model. F11's ordering sentence names line, area and scatter, so for bar the duplicate-x rule is what is checked.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"Node evidence: the scene the controller hands to the renderer, from a three-point shuffled fixture (not the trend fixture), plus the table and keyboard order.\",\n      \"compact\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Chrome compares the drawn SVG for shuffled and sorted input on compact line, area and bar; the Node tests run the same three kinds for order and for the duplicate-x rule.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"F5\",\n    \"statement\": \"No smoothing. A line denser than the screen is simplified so that, for every device-pixel column and every contiguous run of valid samples inside it, the stroke covers exactly that run's minimum and maximum; a break between two runs is kept even inside one column; a slot a series merely has no row for (weekly beside daily) does not break its line; stacked areas are simplified on their cumulative sums; exact values always come from the data, not the drawing.\",\n    \"appliesTo\": [\n      \"line\",\n      \"area\",\n      \"compact\"\n    ],\n    \"notApplicable\": {\n      \"bar\": \"Section 3.6: bars are not simplified when dense; more bars than pixels raises a hint instead (T-dense-bar).\",\n      \"scatter\": \"Section 3.6: scatter is not simplified in 1.0; above 50,000 points a hint says drawing may be slow (T-dense-scatter).\",\n      \"donut\": \"Section 3.6: a donut is not simplified (T-dense-donut).\"\n    },\n    \"evidence\": {\n      \"line\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"property\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-dense.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F5 line: for every generated dense line dataset the drawing keeps each run’s column extrema and its breaks\",\n          \"registration\": \"F5 ${type}: for every generated dense ${kind} dataset the drawing keeps each run’s column extrema and its breaks\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-dense.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F5 line: one outlier in one million stays drawn at DPR 1 and 2 and a dropped sample stays reachable by keyboard and table\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-dense.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F5 line: two peaks separated by a null in one device column remain in separate drawn runs\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-dense.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F5 line: alternating null and valid slots produce isolated markers and no false segments\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-dense.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F5 line: weekly observations connect across daily observations without inventing weekly rows\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-dense.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-dense-line line: two peaks and their gap survive at two zoom levels and two device-pixel ratios\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-dense-line: 100,000 samples at device pixel ratio 1 with fixed 