rer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Node reads which samples the scene's path kept, column by column, at device pixel ratios 1 and 2 and over three x windows (two of them zoomed); tied extremes occur in the generated repeating backgrounds. Chrome reads the SVG path's vertices of a 100,000-sample line: the spike and the dip must lie within one device-pixel column of their own, and the table row it reads (sample 50,001) is not shown to be one the drawing dropped.\",\n      \"area\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. The Node dense areas are always stacked (two series), so the guarantee is checked on cumulative sums, for the upper series' stroke and for its band's upper and lower edges, at device pixel ratios 1 and 2 and three x windows; the dropped-sample readout is checked there too. Chrome draws one unstacked area at device pixel ratios 1 and 2 and one stacked pair at 2, reading the SVG path's vertices with one device-pixel column of tolerance.\",\n      \"compact\": \"Node evidence: compact line and compact area (stacked) are run (a compact bar is not simplified, section 3.6), at device pixel ratios 1 and 2, with three author x domains in place of zoom. A compact chart has no keyboard or table, so the dropped-sample readout does not reach it.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"T-dense-line\",\n    \"statement\": \"Simplified drawing when dense · F5\",\n    \"appliesTo\": [\n      \"line\"\n    ],\n    \"notApplicable\": {\n      \"area\": \"This is the line cell of the section 3.6 row; the area chart has its own cell.\",\n      \"bar\": \"This is the line cell of the section 3.6 row; the bar chart has its own cell.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"This is the line cell of the section 3.6 row; the scatter chart has its own cell.\",\n      \"donut\": \"This is the line cell of the section 3.6 row; the donut chart has its own cell.\",\n      \"compact\": \"Section 3.6 cells c