ith fewer rows beside a denser one (weekly beside daily), so the rule that such a slot does not break its line is untested on area. The one-in-a-million outlier and the alternating valid and missing fixtures run on line only.\"\n    },\n    \"limits\": {\n      \"area\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. The Node dense areas are always stacked (two series), so the guarantee is checked on cumulative sums, for the upper series' stroke and for its band's upper and lower edges, at device pixel ratios 1 and 2 and three x windows; the dropped-sample readout is checked there too. Chrome draws one unstacked area at device pixel ratios 1 and 2 and one stacked pair at 2, reading the SVG path's vertices with one device-pixel column of tolerance.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"T-dense-bar\",\n    \"statement\": \"Simplified drawing when dense · No; more bars than pixels raises a hint\",\n    \"appliesTo\": [\n      \"bar\"\n    ],\n    \"notApplicable\": {\n      \"line\": \"This is the bar cell of the section 3.6 row; the line chart has its own cell.\",\n      \"area\": \"This is the bar cell of the section 3.6 row; the area chart has its own cell.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"This is the bar cell of the section 3.6 row; the scatter chart has its own cell.\",\n      \"donut\": \"This is the bar cell of the section 3.6 row; the donut chart has its own cell.\",\n      \"compact\": \"Section 3.6 cells cover the full charts; the compact variant's rules are in section 3.7 (C2).\"\n    },\n    \"evidence\": {\n      \"bar\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-dense.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-dense-bar bar: more bars than pixels raises AX132 and every rectangle is still drawn\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-dense-bar: more bars than pixels raises the AX132 hint and every bar is still drawn, each where its category is\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"limits\": {\n      \"bar\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Vertical bars on a category axis only: 375 bars in a 240 px container in Node, 2,000 in a 300 px container in Chrome. Chrome checks the hint's level, the count of drawn bars and the place of the one tall bar, not every bar's place.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"T-dense-donut\",\n    \"statement\": \"Simplified drawing when dense · No\",\n    \"appliesTo\": [\n      \"donut\"\n    ],\n    \"notApplicable\": {\n      \"line\": \"This is the donut cell of the section 3.6 row; the line chart has its own cell.\",\n      \"area\": \"This is the donut cell of the section 3.6 row; the area chart has its own cell.\",\n      \"bar\": \"This is the donut cell of the section 3.6 row; the bar chart has its own cell.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"This is the donut cell of the section 3.6 row; the scatter chart has its own cell.\",\n      \"compact\": \"Section 3.6 cells cover the full charts; the compact variant's rules are in section 3.7 (C2).\"\n    },\n    \"evidence\": {\n      \"donut\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-dense.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-dense-donut donut: eight small positive slices retain all eight arcs\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-dense-donut: no simplified drawing: eight slices, the smallest under 0.2 %, are each drawn at their angle in their colour\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"limits\": {\n      \"donut\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. A slice thinner than