ues of the layout. Chrome reads the domains the chart reports through its test hook, for a y reference line above the data. Chrome also reads a y reference band above the data. The x span with half bands is checked at the view stage.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Node evidence: committed domains and the drawn tick values of the layout. Chrome reads the domains the chart reports through its test hook, for a y reference line above the data. Chrome also reads the y domain before and after an x zoom to [12, 22].\",\n      \"compact\": \"Node evidence. The generated-extents and percent/ratio tests run compact line, area and bar; the controller-level reference test runs compact line only; the stack-total test runs compact area and bar.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"F6\",\n    \"statement\": \"Numbers and dates are formatted for the page locale. Ticks and readouts are formatted separately: ticks may be compact (50K); tooltip, table and announcements show the full integer part and the fraction with up to six significant digits, not counting the fraction's leading zeros, with the unit. A custom formatter that throws falls back to the default and raises a diagnostic.\",\n    \"appliesTo\": [\n      \"line\",\n      \"area\",\n      \"bar\",\n      \"scatter\",\n      \"donut\",\n      \"compact\"\n    ],\n    \"notApplicable\": {},\n    \"evidence\": {\n      \"line\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-format.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F6 line: localized readouts keep the full integer and six significant fraction digits, with the unit\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-format.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F6 line: a throwing value formatter falls back for reader text and preserves drawn marks\"\n        },\n        {\n