        \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/f12-note.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F12 donut: one value left out reads correctly for a count of one, and clean data shows no note\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/f12-note.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F12 donut: a readout formatter that throws for one value (AX160) shows a note inside the figure and in the accessibility tree once a reader surface formats that value (reading: the default format in place of the author's is a changed value) (development build)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/f12-note.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F12 donut: a readout formatter that throws for one value (AX160) shows a note inside the figure and in the accessibility tree once a reader surface formats that value (reading: the default format in place of the author's is a changed value) (production build)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/f12-note.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F12 donut: more than eight slices are grouped into \\\"Other (n)\\\" (AX121) and the note says values are shown differently, not that they were left out, in the figure and the accessibility tree\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-disclosure.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F12 donut: three bad values leave a three-value note and summary while the chart preserves the good observations\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-disclosure.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F12 donut: a throwing formatter discloses changed presentation even though the value is still drawn\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/production.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F12 donut: production still reports omitted values in the figure and summary\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"gaps\": {\n      \"line\": \"No test checks the note for AX107 (a date that cannot be parsed leaves its row out); its tests check the summary's count only.\",\n      \"area\": \"No test checks the note for AX107 (a date that cannot be parsed leaves its row out); its tests check the summary's count only.\",\n      \"bar\": \"No test checks the note for AX107 (a date that cannot be parsed leaves its row out); its tests check the summary's count only.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"No test checks the note for AX107 (a date that cannot be parsed leaves its row out); its tests check the summary's count only.\"\n    },\n    \"limits\": {\n      \"line\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. The changed-values tests in Chrome replace the note's text through messages, so the default wording of that note is checked on the Node model only. The count-of-one case is checked in the development build.\",\n      \"area\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. The changed-values tests in Chrome replace the note's text through messages, so the default wording of that note is checked on the Node model only. The count-of-one case is checked in the development build.\",\n      \"bar\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. The changed-values tests in Chrome replace the note's text through messages, so the default wording of that note is checked on the Node model only. The count-of-one case is checked in the development build.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. The changed-values tests in Chrome replace the note's text through messages, so the default wording of that note is checked on the Node model only. The count-of-one case is checked in the development build.\",\n      \"donut\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. The changed-values tests in Chrome replace the note's text through messages, so the default wording of that note is checked on the Node model only. The count-of-one case is checked in the development build.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"F10\",\n    \"statement\": \"Stacks place positive and negative values on their own sides of zero, and the axis covers both totals. The readout's total is the sum when every component has the same sign; with mixed signs it gives the positive total and the negative total, not their net. A missing component is drawn with zero height and the stack is marked \\\"incomplete\\\" in tooltip, table and announcements.\",\n    \"appliesTo\": [\n      \"area\",\n      \"bar\",\n      \"compact\"\n    ],\n    \"notApplicable\": {\n      \"line\": \"Line has no stacked variant.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"Scatter has no stacked variant.\",\n      \"donut\": \"A donut has slices, not stacks.\"\n    },\n    \"evidence\": {\n      \"area\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"property\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-stacks.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F10 area: for any generated mixed-sign area stacks each drawn component uses its own side of zero and the axis covers both sums\",\n          \"registration\": \"F10 ${type}: for any generated mixed-sign ${kind} stacks each drawn component uses its own side of zero and the axis covers both sums\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-stacks.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F10 area: a missing area component has zero height and the reader is told which stack is