ant's rules are in section 3.7 (C2).\"\n    },\n    \"evidence\": {\n      \"donut\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-dense.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-dense-donut donut: eight small positive slices retain all eight arcs\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-dense-donut: no simplified drawing: eight slices, the smallest under 0.2 %, are each drawn at their angle in their colour\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"limits\": {\n      \"donut\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. A slice thinner than 4 px of arc is checked by where its own path starts, not by painted colour.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"T-dense-scatter\",\n    \"statement\": \"Simplified drawing when dense · No in 1.0; above 50,000 points a hint says drawing may be slow\",\n    \"appliesTo\": [\n      \"scatter\"\n    ],\n    \"notApplicable\": {\n      \"line\": \"This is the scatter cell of the section 3.6 row; the line chart has its own cell.\",\n      \"area\": \"This is the scatter cell of the section 3.6 row; the area chart has its own cell.\",\n      \"bar\": \"This is the scatter cell of the section 3.6 row; the bar chart has its own cell.\",\n      \"donut\": \"This is the scatter cell of the section 3.6 row; the donut chart has its own cell.\",\n      \"compact\": \"Section 3.6 cells cover the full charts; the compact variant's rules are in section 3.7 (C2).\"\n    },\n    \"evidence\": {\n      \"scatter\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-dense.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-dense-scatter scatter: the hint starts above 50,000 points and none are simplified away\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-dense-scatter: above 50,000 points the AX133 hint says drawing may be slow, and every point is drawn: points chosen across the data are found at their own positions\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"limits\": {\n      \"scatter\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Chrome counts the drawn point marks (50,001) and finds six chosen points at their positions; Node checks the threshold (no hint at 50,000, AX133 at 50,001).\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"F7\",\n    \"statement\": \"On value axes (y of line, area and bar; both axes of scatter) the zoomed view stays inside the author's domain if given, otherwise inside the automatic domain. A continuous x of line, area or bar spans exactly its data (plus half a band for bars), not padded to a tick. The automatic domain contains all data, the reference lines and bands the chart draws and stack totals, and ends at the first tick at or beyond each extreme; a compact chart draws no reference, so reference has no effect there and is reported as not applicable. A field declared percent (0–100) or ratio (0–1) ends at full scale only when its maximum is at least half of full scale and not above it. Nothing is inferred from a label.\",\n    \"appliesTo\": [\n      \"line\",\n      \"area\",\n      \"bar\",\n      \"scatter\",\n      \"compact\"\n    ],\n    \"notApplicable\": {\n      \"donut\": \"A donut has no axes, so it has no domain.\"\n    },\n    \"evidence\": {\n      \"line\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"property\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-domains.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F7 line: for any generated extents the automatic domain includes data and references and the zoom stays inside its governing domain\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"property\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-domains.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F7 line: for any generated reference extreme the automatic value domain ends at the first drawn tick that reaches it (reading: the tick is the one the reader sees)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-domains.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F7 line: declared percent reaches full scale at half scale while a small maximum uses the first tick\",\n          \"registration\": \"F7 ${type}: declared ${scale} reaches full scale at half scale while a small maximum uses the first tick\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-domains.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F7 line: declared ratio reaches full scale at half scale while a small maximum uses the first tick\",\n          \"registration\": \"F7 ${type}: declared ${scale} reaches full scale at half scale while a small maximum uses the first tick\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/type-matrix.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-zoom-line line: numeric, time and calendar-date fields support zoom on x and Reset restores all observations\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/type-matrix.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-reference-line line: a line and band extend the appropriate domains, bind to reference paint and are listed in summary and caption\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"a line on x 1.1 to 8.9 spans exactly its data (x is not a value axis)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/view/view.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"resolves references against the frame kind and includes value bands and lines in the domain\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-reference-line: a reference line outside the data is included in the domain, painted at its position in the reference colour, labelled next to its own mark, and listed in the summary and the table caption\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"area\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"property\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-domains.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F7 area: for any generated extents the automatic domain includes data and references and the zoom stays inside its governing domain\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"property\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-domains.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F7 area: for any generated reference extreme the automatic value domain ends at the first drawn tick that reaches it (reading: the tick is the one the reader sees)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-domains.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F7 area: declared percent reaches full scale at half scale while a small maximum uses the first tick\",\n          \"registration\": \"F7 ${type}: declared ${scale} reaches full scale at half scale while a small maximum uses the first tick\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-domains.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F7 area: declared ratio reaches full scale at half scale while a small maximum uses the first tick\",\n          \"registration\": \"F7 ${type}: declared ${scale} reaches full scale at half scale while a small maximum uses the first tick\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/type-matrix.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-zoom-area area: numeric, time and calendar-date fields support zoom on x and Reset restores all observations\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/type-matrix.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-reference-area area: a line and band extend the appropriate domains, bind to reference paint and are listed in summary and caption\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"property\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-stacks.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F10 area: for any generated mixed-sign area stacks each drawn component uses its own side of zero and the axis covers both sums\",\n          \"registration\": \"F10 ${type}: for any generated mixed-sign ${kind} stacks each drawn component uses its own side of zero and the axis covers both sums\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-reference-area: a reference line outside the data is included in the domain, painted at its position in the reference colour, labelled next to its own mark, and listed in the summary and the table caption\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"bar\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"property\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-domains.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F7 bar: for any generated extents the automatic domain includes data and references and the zoom stays inside its governing domain\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"property\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-domains.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F7 bar: for any generated reference extreme the automatic value domain ends at the first drawn tick that reaches it (reading: the tick is the one the reader sees)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-domains.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F7 bar: declared percent reaches full scale at half scale while a small maximum uses the first tick\",\n          \"registration\": \"F7 ${type}: declared ${scale} reaches full scale at half scale while a small maximum uses the first tick\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-domains.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F7 bar: declared ratio reaches full scale at half scale while a small maximum uses the first tick\",\n          \"registration\": \"F7 ${type}: declared ${scale} reaches full scale at half scale while a small maximum uses the first tick\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/type-matrix.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-zoom-bar bar: numeric, time and calendar-date fields support zoom on x and Reset restores all observations\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/type-matrix.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-reference-bar bar: a line and band extend the appropriate domains, bind to reference paint and are listed in summary and caption\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"property\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-stacks.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F10 bar: for any generated mixed-sign bar stacks each drawn component uses its own side of zero and the axis covers both sums\",\n          \"registration\": \"F10 ${type}: for any generated mixed-sign ${kind} stacks each drawn component uses its own side of zero and the axis covers both sums\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/scene/scene.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"centers whole continuous bars and retains bands crossing both zoom edges (horizontal false)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/scene/scene.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"pads irregular bar endpoints by their own neighbour spacing and skips non-overlapping bands\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-reference-bar: a reference line outside the data is included in the domain, painted at its position in the reference colour, labelled next to its own mark, and listed in the summary and the table caption\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-reference-bar: a reference band outside the data is included in the domain, painted at its position in the reference colour, labelled next to its own mark, and listed in the summary and the table caption\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"scatter\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"property\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-domains.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F7 scatter: for any generated extents the automatic domain includes data and references and the zoom stays inside its governing domain\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"property\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-domains.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F7 scatter: for any generated reference extreme the automatic value domain ends at the first drawn tick that reaches it (reading: the tick is the one the reader sees)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-domains.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F7 scatter: declared percent reaches full scale at half scale while a small maximum uses the first tick\",\n          \"registration\": \"F7 ${type}: declared ${scale} reaches full scale at half scale while a small maximum uses the first tick\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-domains.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F7 scatter: declared ratio reaches full scale at half scale while a small maximum uses the first tick\",\n          \"registration\": \"F7 ${type}: declared ${scale} reaches full scale at half scale while a small maximum uses the first tick\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/type-matrix.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-zoom-scatter scatter: numeric, time and calendar-date fields support zoom on x and Reset restores all observations\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/type-matrix.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-reference-scatter scatter: a line and band extend the appropriate domains, bind to reference paint and are listed in summary and caption\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"a scatter on x 1.1 to 8.9: the x domain ends at its first and last drawn ticks, which reach the data\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-reference-scatter: a reference line outside the data is included in the domain, painted at its position in the reference colour, labelled next to its own mark, and listed in the summary and the table caption\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-zoom-scatter: x only in 1.0: + narrows the x range, controls are offered, and the y axis keeps the full data range though the visible y extremes change\",\n          \"registration\": \"T-zoom-${type}: ${type === 'scatter' ? 'x only in 1.0: + narrows the x range, controls are offered, and the y axis keeps the full data range though the visible y extremes change' : 'zoom applies: controls are offered and + narrows the x range'}\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"compact\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"property\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-domains.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F7 compact: for any generated extents the automatic domain includes data and references and the zoom stays inside its governing domain\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-domains.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F7 compact: declared percent reaches full scale at half scale while a small maximum uses the first tick\",\n          \"registration\": \"F7 ${type}: declared ${scale} reaches full scale at half scale while a small maximum uses the first tick\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-domains.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F7 compact: declared ratio reaches full scale at half scale while a small maximum uses the first tick\",\n          \"registration\": \"F7 ${type}: declared ${scale} reaches full scale at half scale while a small maximum uses the first tick\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/compact.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"C1 compact line: a reference has no effect on the domain or the description and is reported as not applicable\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/diagnostics/registry.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"AX150 reports the reference option once on compact area\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/diagnostics/registry.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"AX150 reports the reference option once on compact bar\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"property\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-stacks.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F10 compact: for any generated mixed-sign area stacks each drawn component uses its own side of zero and the axis covers both sums\",\n          \"registration\": \"F10 ${type}: for any generated mixed-sign ${kind} stacks each drawn component uses its own side of zero and the axis covers both sums\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"property\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-stacks.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"F10 compact: for any generated mixed-sign bar stacks each drawn component uses its own side of zero and the axis covers both sums\",\n          \"registration\": \"F10 ${type}: for any generated mixed-sign ${kind} stacks each drawn component uses its own side of zero and the axis covers both sums\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"weak\": {\n      \"scatter\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"property\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/layout/layout.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"for any automatic numeric x domain and any width at which the plot is drawn, both ends are drawn ticks\",\n          \"reason\": \"Layout-level property with 300 generated cases, fewer than the 1,000 the spec asks of a property test; it checks only that both x ends are drawn ticks.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"compact\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"property\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/view/view.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"keeps compact area domains independent of references\",\n          \"reason\": \"View stage only, with fast-check's default 100 cases (the spec asks 1,000); the description and the AX150 report are not checked.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"property\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/view/view.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"keeps compact bar domains independent of references\",\n          \"reason\": \"View stage only, with fast-check's default 100 cases (the spec asks 1,000); the description and the AX150 report are not checked.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"gaps\": {\n      \"line\": \"Without an author domain, no test asserts that the y range shown after an x zoom stays inside the automatic domain. The exact x span is tested on a numeric x only, not on a time series.\",\n      \"area\": \"Without an author domain, no test asserts that the y range shown after an x zoom stays inside the automatic domain. No test asserts that an area's continuous x spans exactly its data. Stack totals are shown to lie inside the domain, not that the domain ends at the first tick at or beyond them. No test puts a y reference band beside an area's data.\",\n      \"bar\": \"Without an author domain, no test asserts that the y range shown after an x zoom stays inside the automatic domain. The half-band x span is checked at the view stage on a numeric x only (regular and irregular steps), not on a time series. Stack totals are shown to lie inside the domain, not that the domain ends at the first tick at or beyond them.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"The first-tick ending of x is tested for a number x only; for a date x, view.test.ts asserts that the automatic domain spans exactly the dates, so the rule for a date or time x is not established. A declared percent or ratio scale is tested on y only. No test puts a y reference band beside a scatter's data.\",\n      \"compact\": \"For compact area and bar, that a reference leaves the domain unchanged is shown at the view stage only, that it leaves the description unchanged is not checked, and AX150 is checked at validation only. Whether a compact chart's automatic domain ends at a tick is not asserted: the tick check in f-domains.test.ts skips compact layouts. That a compact chart's x spans exactly its data is not tested.\"\n    },\n    \"limits\": {\n      \"line\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); n