itle\": \"toggling a dark class repaints within a frame, without rebuilding the scene (canvas)\",\n          \"reason\": \"Line, canvas renderer: a class on <html> that darkens the page gives the dark palette's pixels after the first frame, without a new scene; the acceptance suite runs the SVG renderer only.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"area\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/render/theme.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"--axylo-background overrides color-scheme\",\n          \"reason\": \"Renderer level, on a hand-built scene rather than a chart type: with color-scheme: light, --axylo-background: #101418 makes the resolved scheme dark.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"bar\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/render/theme.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"--axylo-background overrides color-scheme\",\n          \"reason\": \"Renderer level, on a hand-built scene rather than a chart type: with color-scheme: light, --axylo-background: #101418 makes the resolved scheme dark.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"scatter\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/render/theme.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"--axylo-background overrides color-scheme\",\n          \"reason\": \"Renderer level, on a hand-built scene rather than a chart type: with color-scheme: light, --axylo-background: #101418 makes the resolved scheme dark.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"donut\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/render/theme.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"--axylo-background overrides color-scheme\",\n          \"reason\": \"Renderer level, on a hand-built scene rather than a chart type: with color-scheme: light, --axylo-background: #101418 makes the resolved scheme dark.\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"compact\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/render/theme.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"--axylo-background overrides color-scheme\",\n          \"reason\": \"Renderer level, on a hand-built scene rather than a chart type: with color-scheme: light, --axylo-background: #101418 makes the resolved scheme dark.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/compact.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"C2 compact area: the scheme comes from the page (L4): a dark page paints the marks in other colours than a light one, and a class toggle repaints them\",\n          \"reason\": \"Compact area: a class on <body> that darkens the page changes the painted mark colour once the chart settles; not timed to one frame, and the color-scheme, override and forced-colour paths are not run.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/compact.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"C2 compact bar: the scheme comes from the page (L4): a dark page paints the marks in other colours than a light one, and a class toggle repaints them\",\n          \"reason\": \"Compact bar: a class on <body> that darkens the page changes the painted mark colour once the chart settles; not timed to one frame, and the color-scheme, override and forced-colour paths are not run.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"gaps\": {\n      \"line\": \"No cited test changes the style of <html> or the contrast preference while a chart is drawn, so those triggers are not checked. The forced-colours switch is read after the chart settles, not in the first frame. --axylo-background is checked overriding the text colour on a chart, and overriding a computed color-scheme only on the renderer's hand-built scene.\",\n      \"area\": \"No cited test changes the style of <html> or the contrast preference while a chart is drawn, so those triggers are not checked. The forced-colours switch is read after the chart settles, not in the first frame. --axylo-background is checked overriding the text colour on a chart, and overriding a computed color-scheme only on the renderer's hand-built scene.\",\n      \"bar\": \"No cited test changes the style of <html> or the contrast preference while a chart is drawn, so those triggers are not checked. The forced-colours switch is read after the chart settles, not in the first frame. --axylo-background is checked overriding the text colour on a chart, and overriding a computed color-scheme only on the renderer's hand-built scene.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"No cited test changes the style of <html> or the contrast preference while a chart is drawn, so those triggers are not checked. The forced-colours switch is read after the chart settles, not in the first frame. --axylo-background is checked overriding the text colour on a chart, and overriding a computed color-scheme only on the renderer's hand-built scene.\",\n      \"donut\": \"No cited test changes the style of <html> or the contrast preference while a chart is drawn, so those triggers are not checked. The forced-colours switch is read after the chart settles, not in the first frame. --axylo-background is checked overriding the text colour on a chart, and overriding a computed color-scheme only on the renderer's hand-built scene.\",\n      \"compact\": \"No cited test changes the style of <html> or the contrast preference while a chart is drawn, so those triggers are not checked. The forced-colours switch is read after the chart settles, not in the first frame. --axylo-background is checked overriding the text colour on a chart, and overriding a computed color-scheme only on the renderer's hand-built scene. Scheme detection, the first-frame triggers and forced colours are checked on a compact line only; for L4, compact area and bar are run in a browser only by the C2 class-toggle test.\"\n    },\n    \"limits\": {\n      \"line\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. First-frame colours are the computed colours of the scene elements in the animation frame after the change; painted pixels are compared after the chart settles, within 24 per channel. Forced colours and the device scheme are Playwright media emulation.\",\n      \"area\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. First-frame colours are the computed colours of the scene elements in the animation frame after the change; painted pixels are compared after the chart settles, within 24 per channel. Forced colours and the device scheme are Playwright media emulation.\",\n      \"bar\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. First-frame colours are the computed colours of the scene elements in the animation frame after the change; painted pixels are compared after the chart settles, within 24 per channel. Forced colours and the device scheme are Playwright media emulation.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. First-frame colours are the computed colours of the scene elements in the animation frame after the change; painted pixels are compared after the chart settles, within 24 per channel. Forced colours and the device scheme are Playwright media emulation.\",\n      \"donut\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. First-frame colours are the computed colours of the scene elements in the animation frame after the change; painted pixels are compared after the chart settles, within 24 per channel. Forced colours and the device scheme are Playwright media emulation.\",\n      \"compact\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. First-frame colours are the computed colours of the scene elements in the animation frame after the change; painted pixels are compared after the chart settles, within 24 per channel. Forced colours and the device scheme are Playwright media emulation. The acceptance L4 tests draw a compact line; the Node test runs compact line, area and bar.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"A6\",\n    \"statement\": \"Content reflows at 320 CSS px and 400% zoom without two-dimensional scrolling, and user text-spacing overrides do not clip text.\",\n    \"appliesTo\": [\n      \"line\",\n      \"area\",\n      \"bar\",\n      \"scatter\",\n      \"donut\",\n      \"compact\"\n    ],\n    \"notApplicable\": {},\n    \"evidence\": {\n      \"line\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A6 line: at 400 % zoom of a 1280 × 1024 window (320 × 256 CSS px at device pixel ratio 4) the page does not scroll horizontally and no chart text is clipped, ellipsised or overlapping (Chrome)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A6 line: with the WCAG 1.4.12 text-spacing overrides no chart text is clipped or pushed outside the figure (Chrome)\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"area\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A6 area: at 400 % zoom of a 1280 × 1024 window (320 × 256 CSS px at device pixel ratio 4) the page does not scroll horizontally and no chart text is clipped, ellipsised or overlapping (Chrome)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A6 area: with the WCAG 1.4.12 text-spacing overrides no chart text is clipped or pushed outside the figure (Chrome)\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"bar\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A6 bar: at 400 % zoom of a 1280 × 1024 window (320 × 256 CSS px at device pixel ratio 4) the page does not scroll horizontally and no chart text is clipped, ellipsised or overlapping (Chrome)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A6 bar: with the WCAG 1.4.12 text-spacing overrides no chart text is clipped or pushed outside the figure (Chrome)\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"scatter\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A6 scatter: at 400 % zoom of a 1280 × 1024 window (320 × 256 CSS px at device pixel ratio 4) the page does not scroll horizontally and no chart text is clipped, ellipsised or overlapping (Chrome)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A6 scatter: with the WCAG 1.4.12 text-spacing overrides no chart text is clipped or pushed outside the figure (Chrome)\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"donut\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A6 donut: at 400 % zoom of a 1280 × 1024 window (320 × 256 CSS px at device pixel ratio 4) the page does not scroll horizontally and no chart text is clipped, ellipsised or overlapping (Chrome)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A6 donut: with the WCAG 1.4.12 text-spacing overrides no chart text is clipped or pushed outside the figure (Chrome)\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"weak\": {\n      \"compact\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/compact.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"C3 compact line: it fills containers of 24×16, 160×48 and 600×120 CSS px, redrawn for each: the five data are evenly spread across the width and their heights keep their order; with no definite height it is 32 px tall\",\n          \"reason\": \"A compact line chart fills containers from 24 × 16 CSS px, so it adds no width of its own; the test uses no 320 CSS px viewport and no text-spacing overrides.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/compact.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"C3 compact area: it fills containers of 24×16, 160×48 and 600×120 CSS px, redrawn for each: the five data are evenly spread across the width and their heights keep their order; with no definite height it is 32 px tall\",\n          \"reason\": \"A compact area chart fills containers from 24 × 16 CSS px, so it adds no width of its own; the test uses no 320 CSS px viewport and no text-spacing overrides.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/compact.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"C3 compact bar: it fills containers of 24×16, 160×48 and 600×120 CSS px, redrawn for each: the five data are evenly spread across the width and their heights keep their order; with no definite height it is 32 px tall\",\n          \"reason\": \"A compact bar chart fills containers from 24 × 16 CSS px, so it adds no width of its own; the test uses no 320 CSS px viewport and no text-spacing overrides.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"gaps\": {\n      \"compact\": \"No test applies the 320 CSS px viewport or the text-spacing overrides to a compact chart, whose visible text is a state message (loading, empty, error) or the corner marker of C5.\"\n    },\n    \"limits\": {\n      \"line\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. The 400 % condition is emulated as a 320 × 256 CSS px viewport at device pixel ratio 4, which is how WCAG 1.4.10 states reflow (320 CSS px wide); the browser's own zoom is not used. Each chart is checked as first drawn, with the table closed and no tooltip. The text-spacing test applies the WCAG 1.4.12 overrides at the default viewport and checks clipping, not overlap.\",\n      \"area\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. The 400 % condition is emulated as a 320 × 256 CSS px viewport at device pixel ratio 4, which is how WCAG 1.4.10 states reflow (320 CSS px wide); the browser's own zoom is not used. Each chart is checked as first drawn, with the table closed and no tooltip. The text-spacing test applies the WCAG 1.4.12 overrides at the default viewport and checks clipping, not overlap.\",\n      \"bar\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. The 400 % condition is emulated as a 320 × 256 CSS px viewport at device pixel ratio 4, which is how WCAG 1.4.10 states reflow (320 CSS px wide); the browser's own zoom is not used. Each chart is checked as first drawn, with the table closed and no tooltip. The text-spacing test applies the WCAG 1.4.12 overrides at the default viewport and checks clipping, not overlap.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. The 400 % condition is emulated as a 320 × 256 CSS px viewport at device pixel ratio 4, which is how WCAG 1.4.10 states reflow (320 CSS px wide); the browser's own zoom is not used. Each chart is checked as first drawn, with the table closed and no tooltip. The text-spacing test applies the WCAG 1.4.12 overrides at the default viewport and checks clipping, not overlap.\",\n      \"donut\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. The 400 % condition is emulated as a 320 × 256 CSS px viewport at device pixel ratio 4, which is how WCAG 1.4.10 states reflow (320 CSS px wide); the browser's own zoom is not used. Each chart is checked as first drawn, with the table closed and no tooltip. The text-spacing test applies the WCAG 1.4.12 overrides at the default viewport and checks clipping, not overlap.\",\n      \"compact\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet.\"\n    },\n    \"pending\": {\n      \"line\": \"No Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet: the criterion asks for the viewport and text-spacing tests in three engines.\",\n      \"area\": \"No Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet: the criterion asks for the viewport and text-spacing tests in three engines.\",\n      \"bar\": \"No Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet: the criterion asks for the viewport and text-spacing tests in three engines.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"No Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet: the criterion asks for the viewport and text-spacing tests in three engines.\",\n      \"donut\": \"No Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet: the criterion asks for the viewport and text-spacing tests in three engines.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"I1\",\n    \"statement\": \"Pointing anywhere in the plot shows what is there, by the type's picking rule (section 3.6), within one frame at the 95th percentile. On line, area and bar the tooltip lists every visible series at the nearest x; a series with no row there reads \\\"No observation\\\", distinct from \\\"No data\\\". The tooltip stays inside the viewport, covers neither the active mark nor any control, can itself be hovered, and lists at most eight rows plus \\\"+N more\\\". A plot narrower than 240 px or shorter than 140 px shows the same content as text in a strip reserved under it; where the strip would leave the plot under the minimum of L8, pointing highlights the datum without a readout. Escape closes it until the pointer reaches a different datum.\",\n    \"appliesTo\": [\n      \"line\",\n      \"area\",\n      \"bar\",\n      \"scatter\",\n      \"donut\"\n    ],\n    \"notApplicable\": {\n      \"compact\": \"Section 3.7: a compact chart has no tooltip, and C1 gives it no pointer-only behaviour.\"\n    },\n    \"evidence\": {\n      \"line\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I1 line: at 20 positions, the four edges included, what is there is shown by the type's picking rule within one frame of the move (95th percentile, counted in animation frames), inside the viewport, without covering the active mark\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I1 line: the tooltip can itself be hovered (decision 0004 revision 2, rule 3b): after a 300 ms rest on the datum, moving straight onto the tooltip's rectangle, it stays for the same datum (same rows) and does not move at every step; with the pointer inside it, it is still shown; Escape closes it until another datum\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I1 line: outside readout mode a tooltip never overlaps a control, shown for the pointer or for the keyboard\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I1 line: readout mode is decided by layout: on each side of the 240 px width limit (the plot jumps across it when the strip is reserved), a plot at or above it gets a floating tooltip and one below it gets the content in a strip reserved under the plot, with no floating tooltip; showing or hiding a datum moves nothing; the strip covers nothing and nothing covers it\",\n          \"registration\": \"I1 ${type}: readout mode is decided by layout: on each side of the ${axis === 'width' ? '240 px width' : '140 px height'} limit (the plot jumps across it when the strip is reserved), a plot at or above it gets a floating tooltip and one below it gets the content in a strip reserved under the plot, with no floating tooltip; showing or hiding a datum moves nothing; the strip covers nothing and nothing covers it\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I1 line: readout mode is decided by layout: on each side of the 140 px height limit (the plot jumps across it when the strip is reserved), a plot at or above it gets a floating tooltip and one below it gets the content in a strip reserved under the plot, with no floating tooltip; showing or hiding a datum moves nothing; the strip covers nothing and nothing covers it\",\n          \"registration\": \"I1 ${type}: readout mode is decided by layout: on each side of the ${axis === 'width' ? '240 px width' : '140 px height'} limit (the plot jumps across it when the strip is reserved), a plot at or above it gets a floating tooltip and one below it gets the content in a strip reserved under the plot, with no floating tooltip; showing or hiding a datum moves nothing; the strip covers nothing and nothing covers it\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/bro