dges included, what is there is shown by the type's picking rule within one frame of the move (95th percentile, counted in animation frames), inside the viewport, without covering the active mark\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I1 area: the tooltip can itself be hovered (decision 0004 revision 2, rule 3b): after a 300 ms rest on the datum, moving straight onto the tooltip's rectangle, it stays for the same datum (same rows) and does not move at every step; with the pointer inside it, it is still shown; Escape closes it until another datum\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I1 area: outside readout mode a tooltip never overlaps a control, shown for the pointer or for the keyboard\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I1 area: readout mode is decided by layout: on each side of the 240 px width limit (the plot jumps across it when the strip is reserved), a plot at or above it gets a floating tooltip and one below it gets the content in a strip reserved under the plot, with no floating tooltip; showing or hiding a datum moves nothing; the strip covers nothing and nothing covers it\",\n          \"registration\": \"I1 ${type}: readout mode is decided by layout: on each side of the ${axis === 'width' ? '240 px width' : '140 px height'} limit (the plot jumps across it when the strip is reserved), a plot at or above it gets a floating tooltip and one below it gets the content in a strip reserved under the plot, with no floating tooltip; showing or hiding a datum moves nothing; the strip covers nothing and nothing covers it\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"k