e the strip keeps the strip, 79.9 px gives the mode with no readout. Nothing is rendered.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"gaps\": {\n      \"line\": \"Where the strip would leave the plot under the 80 px minimum of L8, the cited tests show no strip, no floating tooltip and a hover event; that the datum is visibly highlighted with no readout is not asserted.\",\n      \"area\": \"No test runs this chart type where the strip would leave the plot under the 80 px minimum of L8, the case in which pointing must highlight the datum with no readout.\",\n      \"bar\": \"No test runs this chart type where the strip would leave the plot under the 80 px minimum of L8, the case in which pointing must highlight the datum with no readout.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"No test runs this chart type where the strip would leave the plot under the 80 px minimum of L8, the case in which pointing must highlight the datum with no readout.\",\n      \"donut\": \"No test runs this chart type where the strip would leave the plot under the 80 px minimum of L8, the case in which pointing must highlight the datum with no readout. That the tooltip leaves the whole active slice uncovered is not asserted: the 20-position test checks only the 12 px square under the pointer.\"\n    },\n    \"limits\": {\n      \"line\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Latency is counted in animation frames from the pointer move to the next change of the tooltip or strip, over the 20 probes; P4 covers large data. The hover test rests 300 ms on the datum before moving onto the tooltip (decision 0004, rule 3b). Controls are taken by their boxes (buttons, legend entries, inputs); a control's painted focus outline is checked once, on a line (final-closing).\",\n      \"area\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Latency is counted in animation frames from the pointer move to the next change of the tooltip or strip, over the 20 probes; P4 covers large data. The hover test rests 300 ms on the datum before moving onto the tooltip (decision 0004, rule 3b). Controls are taken by their boxes (buttons, legend entries, inputs), not with their focus outlines.\",\n      \"bar\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Latency is counted in animation frames from the pointer move to the next change of the tooltip or strip, over the 20 probes; P4 covers large data. The hover test rests 300 ms on the datum before moving onto the tooltip (decision 0004, rule 3b). Controls are taken by their boxes (buttons, legend entries, inputs), not with their focus outlines.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Latency is counted in animation frames from the pointer move to the next change of the tooltip or strip, over the 20 probes; P4 covers large data. The hover test rests 300 ms on the datum before moving onto the tooltip (decision 0004, rule 3b). The probes sit on and up to 12 px from five of the six points, not along the plot's edges; the 24 px radius and ties are in T-pointer-scatter. Controls are taken by their boxes (buttons, legend entries, inputs), not with their focus outlines.\",\n      \"donut\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Latency is counted in animation frames from the pointer move to the next change of the tooltip or strip, over the 20 probes; P4 covers large data. The hover test rests 300 ms on the datum before moving onto the tooltip (decision 0004, rule 3b). The probes lie on the ring at 85% of its outer radius, not along the plot's edges; the hole and the outside are in T-pointer-donut. A donut tooltip names one slice, so the eight-row limit cannot arise. Controls are taken by their boxes (buttons, legend entries, inputs), not with their focus outlines.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"T-pointer-line\",\n    \"statement\": \"Picking by pointer · Nearest x\",\n    \"appliesTo\": [\n      \"line\"\n    ],\n    \"notApplicable\": {\n      \"area\": \"This is the line cell of section 3.6.\",\n      \"bar\": \"This is the line cell of section 3.6.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"This is the line cell of section 3.6.\",\n      \"donut\": \"This is the line cell of section 3.6.\",\n      \"compact\": \"Section 3.7: a compact chart has no tooltip, and C1 gives it no pointer-only behaviour.\"\n    },\n    \"evidence\": {\n      \"line\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/type-matrix.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-pointer-line line: picks the nearest x regardless of pointer height\",\n          \"registration\": \"T-pointer-${kind} ${kind}: picks ${kind === 'bar' ? 'the category band under the pointer at either edge' : 'the nearest x regardless of pointer height'}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-pointer-line: the pointer picks the nearest x: 30 % of the way from one day to the next shows the first, 70 % the second\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"limits\": {\n      \"line\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. The browser test points 30% and 70% of the way between two days, near the plot's top; the Node test points a quarter of the way to a neighbour, at the plot's top and bottom edges.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"T-pointer-area\",\n    \"statement\": \"Picking by pointer · Nearest x\",\n    \"appliesTo\": [\n      \"area\"\n    ],\n    \"notApplicable\": {\n      \"line\": \"This is the area cell of section 3.6.\",\n      \"bar\": \"This is the area cell of section 3.6.\",\n      \"scatt