 {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a5-not-colour-alone.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A5 compact: two compact series differ by dash as well as colour, with no legend to tell them apart\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/compact.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"C4 compact area: two series differ by dash as well as colour, and AX131 suggests one series per compact chart\",\n          \"registration\": \"C4 compact ${kind}: two series differ by ${kind === 'bar' ? 'more than colour, as painted (reading: A5 asks a non-colour cue of bars too)' : 'dash as well as colour'}, and AX131 suggests one series per compact chart\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/compact.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"C4 compact bar: two series differ by more than colour, as painted (reading: A5 asks a non-colour cue of bars too), and AX131 suggests one series per compact chart\",\n          \"registration\": \"C4 compact ${kind}: two series differ by ${kind === 'bar' ? 'more than colour, as painted (reading: A5 asks a non-colour cue of bars too)' : 'dash as well as colour'}, and AX131 suggests one series per compact chart\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a5-not-colour-alone.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A5 compact: under prefers-contrast: more three lines differ by dash, pairwise\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a5-not-colour-alone.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A5 compact: under forced-colors: active three lines differ by dash, pairwise\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a5-not-colour-alone.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A5 compact: the eight painted colours (light scheme) are each at least 3:1 on their painted backdrop and at least 0.10 apart in OKLab under normal vision and simulated protanopia, deuteranopia and tritanopia, analytic and as an 8-bit image\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a5-not-colour-alone.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A5 compact: the eight painted colours (dark scheme) are each at least 3:1 on their painted backdrop and at least 0.10 apart in OKLab under normal vision and simulated protanopia, deuteranopia and tritanopia, analytic and as an 8-bit image\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a5-not-colour-alone.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A5 compact: on a background the palette does not suit (the first series' painted colour itself), AX141 is raised\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"gaps\": {\n      \"bar\": \"No test asserts that the bars within a group are drawn in the order in which the legend and the tooltip list the series: the tooltip test asserts the names and their order, and the separator tests the distinct positions.\",\n      \"compact\": \"Compact area and compact bar are not checked under prefers-contrast: more or forced colours, and the palette scores and AX141 run on compact line only. No test measures separators between adjacent filled marks in a stacked compact area or bar. The fill-pattern check uses two series, so the rule for series further apart (four patterns) is not exercised.\"\n    },\n    \"limits\": {\n      \"line\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Markers are found in the SVG and their shapes compared with the legend and tooltip swatches; dashes are computed styles; palette colours are sampled from painted marks against the painted backdrop, with the colour-vision deficiencies simulated analytically and on an 8-bit image; AX141 is checked on one background, the first series' own colour. Whether a reader can follow three crossing lines in grayscale is a human judgement; the test compares marker shape classes.\",\n      \"area\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Markers are found in the SVG and their shapes compared with the legend and tooltip swatches; dashes are computed styles; the separator is measured on painted pixels against a 1 px control gap; palette colours are sampled from painted marks against the painted backdrop, with the colour-vision deficiencies simulated analytically and on an 8-bit image; AX141 is checked on one background, the first series' own colour.\",\n      \"bar\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Separators are measured on painted pixels against a 1 px control gap (stacked bars vertical only, grouped bars both ways); palette colours are sampled from painted marks against the painted backdrop, with the colour-vision deficiencies simulated analytically and on an 8-bit image; AX141 is checked on one background, the first series' own colour.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Point shapes are compared in the SVG and in the legend and tooltip swatches; palette colours are sampled from painted marks against the painted backdrop, with the colour-vision deficiencies simulated analytically and on an 8-bit image; AX141 is checked on one background, the first series' own colour.\",\n      \"donut\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Seams are measured on painted pixels against a 1 px control gap at the same angle, in the light scheme; palette colours are sampled from painted marks against the painted backdrop, with the colour-vision deficiencies simulated analytically and on an 8-bit image; AX141 is checked on one background, the first series' own colour.\",\n      \"compact\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Dashes are computed styles; the compact bar pattern is measured as painted texture inside the bars; palette colours are sampled from painted marks against the painted backdrop, with the colour-vision deficiencies simulated analytically and on an 8-bit image; AX141 is checked on one background, the first series' own colour.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"L2\",\n    \"statement\": \"Text is at least 12 CSS px and at least 4.5:1 against what is behind it, including text drawn inside a mark and legend entries for hidden series. Marks, axis lines and focus indicators are at least 3:1; gridlines are exempt. Holds in light and dark.\",\n    \"appliesTo\": [\n      \"line\",\n      \"area\",\n      \"bar\",\n      \"scatter\",\n      \"donut\",\n      \"compact\"\n    ],\n    \"notApplicable\": {},\n    \"evidence\": {\n      \"line\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/l-legibility.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"L2 line: in the light scheme every text is at least 12 CSS px and 4.5:1 on what is painted behind it (legend entries of hidden series included); marks, axis lines and the focus indicator are painted at least 3:1\",\n          \"registration\": \"L2 ${type}: in the ${scheme} scheme every text is at least 12 CSS px and 4.5:1 on what is painted behind it (legend entries of hidden series included); marks${type === 'compact' ? '' : ', axis lines and the focus indicator'} are painted at least 3:1\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/accepta