tate is announced exactly once, politely, and nothing else is\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/reader-model.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"L7 compact: loading, empty and error draw no data marks and each state change is announced once\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"gaps\": {\n      \"compact\": \"Compact area and bar are checked only through the controller (Node): the message, no marks or labels, and one announcement per change. Their painted message and its place in the tile are not checked in a browser, and their internal-failure state is not checked at all.\"\n    },\n    \"limits\": {\n      \"line\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. The acceptance test counts distinct announced texts, so an identical announcement repeated would not be seen; the Node test counts every announcement, through the controller. A change into the empty state is announced-checked only through the controller (Node), without politeness. The line suite's loading test records every change of the polite region.\",\n      \"area\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. The acceptance test counts distinct announced texts, so an identical announcement repeated would not be seen; the Node test counts every announcement, through the controller. A change into the empty state is announced-checked only through the controller (Node), without politeness.\",\n      \"bar\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. The acceptance test counts distinct announced texts, so an identical announcement repeated would not be seen; the Node test counts every announcement, through the controller. A change into the empty state is announced-checked only through the controller (Node), without politeness.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. The acceptance test counts distinct announced texts, so an identical announcement repeated would not be seen; the Node test counts every announcement, through the controller. A change into the empty state is announced-checked only through the controller (Node), without politeness.\",\n      \"donut\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. The acceptance test counts distinct announced texts, so an identical announcement repeated would not be seen; the Node test counts every announcement, through the controller. A change into the empty state is announced-checked only through the controller (Node), without politeness.\",\n      \"compact\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. The acceptance test counts distinct announced texts, so an identical announcement repeated would not be seen; the Node test counts every announcement, through the controller. A change into the empty state is announced-checked only through the controller (Node), without politeness. The browser tests draw a compact line.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"L8\",\n    \"statement\": \"When the figure cannot hold a readable plot (less than 120 × 80 CSS px for the plot), it shows instead the title, a short summary (the first sentence of the generated summary on at most two lines, cut with an ellipsis beyond that; the full summary remains the figure's description) and the table control, and raises AX142.\",\n    \"appliesTo\": [\n      \"line\",\n      \"area\",\n      \"bar\",\n      \"scatter\",\n      \"donut\"\n    ],\n    \"notApplicable\": {\n      \"compact\": \"A compact chart has no title, summary text or table control to fall back to; it draws at any size from 24 × 16 CSS px (C3).\"\n    },\n    \"evidence\": {\n      \"line\": [\n        {\n  