      {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/type-matrix.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-zoom-donut donut: even an explicit zoom call leaves arc angles and table rows in slice order\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"limits\": {\n      \"donut\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. No zoom control is shown; +, - and the wheel leave the drawing unchanged, and the Node test calls zoom() directly. A drag or a pinch over the donut is not tried.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"T-zoom-scatter\",\n    \"statement\": \"Zoom · Yes, both axes later; x only in 1.0\",\n    \"appliesTo\": [\n      \"scatter\"\n    ],\n    \"notApplicable\": {\n      \"line\": \"This is the scatter cell of section 3.6.\",\n      \"area\": \"This is the scatter cell of section 3.6.\",\n      \"bar\": \"This is the scatter cell of section 3.6.\",\n      \"donut\": \"This is the scatter cell of section 3.6.\",\n      \"compact\": \"Section 3.7: a compact chart has no zoom.\"\n    },\n    \"evidence\": {\n      \"scatter\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-zoom-scatter: x only in 1.0: + narrows the x range, controls are offered, and the y axis keeps the full data range though the visible y extremes change\",\n          \"registration\": \"T-zoom-${type}: ${type === 'scatter' ? 'x only in 1.0: + narrows the x range, controls are offered, and the y axis keeps the full data range though the visible y extremes change' : 'zoom applies: controls are offered and + narrows the x range'}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I3 scatter: from the keyboard, each of +, Shift+Right, Shift+Left, - and 0 has its own effect, checked after each key\",\n          \"registration\": \"I3 ${cell(type)}${type === 'bar (date)' ? ' (date axis)' : type === 'bar' ? ' (number axis)' : ''}: from the keyboard, each of +, Shift+Right, Shift+Left, - and 0 has its own effect, checked after each key\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/type-matrix.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"T-zoom-scatter scatter: numeric, time and calendar-date fields support zoom on x and Reset restores all observations\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"gaps\": {\n      \"scatter\": \"That zoom reaches x only (no control or gesture zooms y) is not asserted: the T-zoom browser test zooms through the public zoom() call, and its y check uses a window whose visible y extremes equal the full ones; the I3 tests read only the x range. On a time or date x a scatter chart is zoomed only through the Node controller's zoom().\"\n    },\n    \"limits\": {\n      \"scatter\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. In the browser, zoom runs on a numeric x.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"I4\",\n    \"statement\": \"Every interaction works with a single pointer without dragging (the Select range toggle lets two clicks set a zoom range) and by touch. Every control is at least 24 × 24 CSS px. A one-finger drag on a chart scrolls the page.\",\n    \"appliesTo\": [\n      \"line\",\n      \"area\",\n      \"bar\",\n      \"scatter\",\n      \"donut\"\n    ],\n    \"notApplicable\": {\n      \"compact\": \"Section 3.7 and C1: a compact chart has no controls and no pointer-only behaviour, so there is nothing to operate or measure. No test drags a finger over a compact chart; the notes raise whether the scroll clause reaches it.\"\n    },\n    \"evidence\": {\n      \"line\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I4 line: Select range is a toggle of at least 24 × 24 CSS px after Zoom in in the roving order; Enter and Space toggle aria-pressed, Escape releases it; pressed, two clicks without a drag set the x range they span, and the same clicks unpressed leave the range alone\",\n          \"registration\": \"I4 ${cell(type)}${type === 'bar (date)' ? ' (date axis)' : type === 'bar' ? ' (number axis)' : ''}: Select range is a toggle of at least 24 × 24 CSS px after Zoom in in the roving order; Enter and Space toggle aria-pressed, Escape releases it; pressed, two clicks without a drag set the x range they span, and the same clicks unpressed leave the range alone\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I3 line: by single clicks only: Zoom in twice quarters the range, Zoom out doubles it, Pan right reaches the end, Reset returns\",\n          \"registration\": \"I3 ${cell(type)}${type === 'bar (date)' ? ' (date axis)' : type === 'bar' ? ' (number axis)' : ''}: by single clicks only: Zoom in twice quarters the range, Zoom out doubles it, Pan right reaches the end, Reset returns\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I4 line: every control is at least 24 × 24 CSS px: toolbar, legend, table pager, jump field, the rows of a pinned tooltip and the readout strip's entries for a pinned datum (hovered rows are text, decision 0004)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/a11y/axe.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"every control and the focus indicator are visible in forced colors; nothing animates under reduced motion\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axy