ases it; pressed, two clicks without a drag set the x range they span, and the same clicks unpressed leave the range alone\",\n          \"registration\": \"I4 ${cell(type)}${type === 'bar (date)' ? ' (date axis)' : type === 'bar' ? ' (number axis)' : ''}: Select range is a toggle of at least 24 × 24 CSS px after Zoom in in the roving order; Enter and Space toggle aria-pressed, Escape releases it; pressed, two clicks without a drag set the x range they span, and the same clicks unpressed leave the range alone\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I4 bar (date axis): Select range is a toggle of at least 24 × 24 CSS px after Zoom in in the roving order; Enter and Space toggle aria-pressed, Escape releases it; pressed, two clicks without a drag set the x range they span, and the same clicks unpressed leave the range alone\",\n          \"registration\": \"I4 ${cell(type)}${type === 'bar (date)' ? ' (date axis)' : type === 'bar' ? ' (number axis)' : ''}: Select range is a toggle of at least 24 × 24 CSS px after Zoom in in the roving order; Enter and Space toggle aria-pressed, Escape releases it; pressed, two clicks without a drag set the x range they span, and the same clicks unpressed leave the range alone\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I3 bar (number axis): by single clicks only: Zoom in twice quarters the range, Zoom out doubles it, Pan right reaches the end, Reset returns\",\n          \"registration\": \"I3 ${cell(type)}${type === 'bar (date)' ? ' (date axis)' : type === 'bar' ? ' (number axis)' : ''}: by single clicks only: Zoom in twice quarters the range, Zoom out doubles it, Pan right reaches the end, Reset returns\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I3 bar (date axis): by single clicks only: Zoom in twice quarters the range, Zoom out doubles it, Pan right reaches the end, Reset returns\",\n          \"registration\": \"I3 ${cell(type)}${type === 'bar (date)' ? ' (date axis)' : type === 'bar' ? ' (number axis)' : ''}: by single clicks only: Zoom in twice quarters the range, Zoom out doubles it, Pan right reaches the end, Reset returns\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I4 bar: every control is at least 24 × 24 CSS px: toolbar, legend, table pager, jump field, the rows of a pinned tooltip and the readout strip's entries for a pinned datum (hovered rows are text, decision 0004)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I4 bar: by touch alone: a tap shows what is under the finger, taps operate the legend toggle, Zoom in where it applies, and the table control, and a one-finger vertical drag over the chart scrolls the page from where it was\",\n          \"registration\": \"I4 ${type}: by touch alone: a tap shows what is under the finger, taps operate the ${type === 'donut' ? 'table control' : 'legend toggle, Zoom in where it applies, and the table control'}, and a one-finger vertical drag over the chart scrolls the page from where it was\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"scatter\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I4 scatter: Select range is a toggle of at least 24 × 24 CSS px after Zoom in in the roving order; Enter and Space toggle aria-pressed, Escape releases it; pressed, two clicks without a drag set the x range they span, and the same clicks unpressed leave the range alone\",\n          \"registration\": \"I4 ${cell(type)}${type === 'bar (date)' ? ' (date axis)' : type === 'bar' ? ' (number axis)' : ''}: Select range is a toggle of at least 24 × 24 CSS px after Zoom in in the roving order; Enter and Space toggle aria-pressed, Escape releases it; pressed, two clicks without a drag set the x range they span, and the same clicks unpressed leave the range alone\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I3 scatter: by single clicks only: Zoom in twice quarters the range, Zoom out doubles it, Pan right reaches the end, Reset returns\",\n          \"registration\": \"I3 ${cell(type)}${type === 'bar (date)' ? ' (date axis)' : type === 'bar' ? ' (number axis)' : ''}: by single clicks only: Zoom in twice quarters the range, Zoom out doubles it, Pan right reaches the end, Reset returns\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I4 scatter: every control is at least 24 × 24 CSS px: toolbar, legend, table pager, jump field, the rows of a pinned tooltip and the readout strip's entries for a pinned datum (hovered rows are text, decision 0004)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I4 scatter: by touch alone: a tap shows what is under the finger, taps operate the legend toggle, Zoom in where it applies, and the table control, and a one-finger vertical drag over the chart scrolls the page from where it was\",\n          \"registration\": \"I4 ${type}: by touch alone: a tap shows what is under the finger, taps operate the ${type === 'donut' ? 'table control' : 'legend toggle, Zoom in where it applies, and the table control'}, and a one-finger vertical drag over the chart scrolls the page from where it was\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"donut\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I4 donut: every control is at least 24 × 24 CSS px: toolbar, legend, table pager, jump field, the rows of a pinned tooltip and the readout strip's entries for a pinned datum (hovered rows are text, decision 0004)\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I4 donut: by touch alone: a tap shows what is under the finger, taps operate the table control, and a one-finger vertical drag over the chart scrolls the page from where it was\",\n          \"registration\": \"I4 ${type}: by touch alone: a tap shows what is under the finger, taps operate the ${type === 'donut' ? 'table control' : 'legend toggle, Zoom in where it applies, and the table control'}, and a one-finger vertical drag over the chart scrolls the page from where it was\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"gaps\": {\n      \"line\": \"Sizes: the table's pager and jump field are hidden on the fixtures' one-page tables, so they are not measured, and Resume is not measured. Touch: Pause and Resume, Pan, Reset, the table pager and the jump field are not shown to work by touch.\",\n      \"area\": \"Sizes: the table's pager and jump field are hidden on the fixtures' one-page tables, so they are not measured, and neither are Reset zoom, Pan left and Pan right (shown only while zoomed) or Resume. Touch: Select range, Pause and Resume, Pan, Reset, a pinned tooltip's rows, the table pager and the jump field are not shown to work by touch.\",\n      \"bar\": \"Sizes: the size test runs the category bar fixture, which has no zoom controls, so on number and date bars only the Select range toggle is measured; the table's pager and jump field are hidden on the fixtures' one-page tables, so they are not measured, and Resume is not measured. Touch: zoom on a number or date bar, Pause and Resume, a pinned tooltip's rows, the table pager and the jump field are not shown to work by touch.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"Sizes: the table's pager and jump field are hidden on the fixtures' one-page tables, so they are not measured, and neither are Reset zoom, Pan left and Pan right (shown only while zoomed) or Resume. Touch: Select range, Pause and Resume, Pan, Reset, a pinned tooltip's rows, the table pager and the jump field are not shown to work by touch.\",\n      \"donut\": \"Sizes: the table's pager and jump field are hidden on the fixtures' one-page tables, so they are not measured, and Resume is not measured. Touch: the slice list's entries, a pinned tooltip's row, Pause and Resume, the table pager and the jump field are not shown to work by touch.\"\n    },\n    \"limits\": {\n      \"line\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Touch is emulated: taps through Playwright's touchscreen on a touch-enabled page, the one-finger drag through CDP touch events; no physical touch device is used. Sizes are each element's own bounding rectangle in CSS px. The forced-colours test measures the zoomed, streaming toolbar of a line on a time x.\",\n      \"area\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Touch is emulated: taps through Playwright's touchscreen on a touch-enabled page, the one-finger drag through CDP touch events; no physical touch device is used. Sizes are each element's own bounding rectangle in CSS px.\",\n      \"bar\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Touch is emulated: taps through Playwright's touchscreen on a touch-enabled page, the one-finger drag through CDP touch events; no physical touch device is used. Sizes are each element's own bounding rectangle in CSS px.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Touch is emulated: taps through Playwright's touchscreen on a touch-enabled page, the one-finger drag through CDP touch events; no physical touch device is used. Sizes are each element's own bounding rectangle in CSS px.\",\n      \"donut\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Touch is emulated: taps through Playwright's touchscreen on a touch-enabled page, the one-finger drag through CDP touch events; no physical touch device is used. Sizes are each element's own bounding rectangle in CSS px.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"A7\",\n    \"statement\": \"Data arriving does not speak. Announcements happen only for the reader's own navigation and for a change of state (L7). While data streams, keyboard focus stays on the same datum until it leaves the window.\",\n    \"appliesTo\": [\n      \"line\",\n      \"area\",\n      \"bar\",\n      \"scatter\",\n      \"donut\",\n      \"compact\"\n    ],\n    \"notApplicable\": {},\n    \"evidence\": {\n      \"line\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/reader-model.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A7 line: appended data is quiet and the lookup resolves a reader’s datum until it leaves the window\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A7 line: 24 charts appending ten times each change no live region, with no chart focused\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A7 line: with the plot focused, a sliding window keeps focus on its datum: the value text is not rewritten while the datum stays (decision 0004), the numeric position follows it, eviction moves focus to the next datum once, and the next key reads the current count\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"area\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/reader-model.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A7 area: appended data is quiet and the lookup resolves a reader’s datum until it leaves the window\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A7 area: 24 charts appending ten times each change no live region, with no chart focused\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A7 area: with the plot focused, a sliding window keeps focus on its datum: the value text is not rewritten while the datum stays (decision 0004), the numeric position follows it, eviction moves focus to the next datum once, and the next key reads the current count\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"bar\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/reader-model.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A7 bar: appended data is quiet and the lookup resolves a reader’s datum until it leaves the window\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A7 bar: 24 charts appending ten times each change no live region, with no chart focused\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A7 bar: with the plot focused, a sliding window keeps focus on its datum: the value text is not rewritten while the datum stays (decision 0004), the numeric position follows it, eviction moves focus to the next datum once, and the next key reads the current count\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"scatter\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/reader-model.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A7 scatter: appended data is quiet and the lookup resolves a reader’s datum until it leaves the window\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A7 scatter: 24 charts appending ten times each change no live region, with no chart focused\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A7 scatter: with the plot focused, a sliding window keeps focus on its datum: the value text is not rewritten while the datum stays (decision 0004), the numeric position follows it, eviction moves focus to the next datum once, and the next key reads the current count\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"donut\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/reader-model.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A7 donut: appended data is quiet and the lookup resolves a reader’s datum until it leaves the window\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A7 donut: 24 charts appending ten times each change no live region, with no chart focused\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/a6-a10.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A7 donut: with the plot focused, a sliding window keeps focus on its datum: the value text is not rewritten while the datum stays (decision 0004), the numeric position follows it, eviction moves focus to the next datum once, and the next key reads the current count\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"compact\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/reader-model.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"A7 compact: appends update the static summary quietly in line, area and bar\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"gaps\": {\n      \"compact\": \"Only the Node model is checked: across an append in compact line, area and bar it announces nothing and updates the summary. No browser test watches a compact chart's live regions while it streams, alone or 24 at a time.\"\n    },\n    \"limits\": {\n      \"line\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Live regions are watched as DOM mutations (aria-live other than off, role status, alert or log), not as speech. The plot's focus is read as the document's active element and its numeric position from Chrome's accessibility tree; the value text is read from the DOM attribute aria-valuetext, and decision 0004 part 2 sets when it may be rewritten.\",\n      \"area\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Live regions are watched as DOM mutations (aria-live other than off, role status, alert or log), not as speech. The plot's focus is read as the document's active element and its numeric position from Chrome's accessibility tree; the value text is read from the DOM attribute aria-valuetext, and decision 0004 part 2 sets when it may be rewritten.\",\n      \"bar\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Live regions are watched as DOM mutations (aria-live other than off, role status, alert or log), not as speech. The plot's focus is read as the document's active element and its numeric position from Chrome's accessibility tree; the value text is read from the DOM attribute aria-valuetext, and decision 0004 part 2 sets when it may be rewritten.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Live regions are watched as DOM mutations (aria-live other than off, role status, alert or log), not as speech. The plot's focus is read as the document's active element and its numeric position from Chrome's accessibility tree; the value text is read from the DOM attribute aria-valuetext, and decision 0004 part 2 sets when it may be rewritten.\",\n      \"donut\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Live regions are watched as DOM mutations (aria-live other than off, role status, alert or log), not as speech. The plot's focus is read as the document's active element and its numeric position from Chrome's accessibility tree; the value text is read from the DOM attribute aria-valuetext, and decision 0004 part 2 sets when it may be rewritten. On a donut every append changes the focused slice's share, so the test compares the slice's own name and value while it stays, not the whole text.\",\n      \"compact\": \"A compact chart has no tab stop (C1), so the focus part does not reach it.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"I6\",\n    \"statement\": \"A chart fed by append shows a Pause/Resume control. While paused, new rows are buffered and the view does not move.\",\n    \"appliesTo\": [\n      \"line\",\n      \"area\",\n      \"bar\",\n      \"scatter\",\n      \"donut\"\n    ],\n    \"notApplicable\": {\n      \"compact\": \"Section 3.7: a compact chart draws marks only, with no toolbar, so it has no Pause/Resume control.\"\n    },\n    \"evidence\": {\n      \"line\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I6 line: append shows a Pause control; paused, new rows are buffered and nothing a reader gets moves (marks, summary, value text, tooltip, open table); Resume applies each buffered row once, with its values\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"area\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I6 area: append shows a Pause control; paused, new rows are buffered and nothing a reader gets moves (marks, summary, value text, tooltip, open table); Resume applies each buffered row once, with its values\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"bar\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I6 bar: append shows a Pause control; paused, new rows are buffered and nothing a reader gets moves (marks, summary, value text, tooltip, open table); Resume applies each buffered row once, with its values\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"scatter\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I6 scatter: append shows a Pause control; paused, new rows are buffered and nothing a reader gets moves (marks, summary, value text, tooltip, open table); Resume applies each buffered row once, with its values\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"donut\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I6 donut: append shows a Pause control; paused, new rows are buffered and nothing a reader gets moves (marks, summary, value text, tooltip, open table); Resume applies each buffered row once, with its values\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"limits\": {\n      \"line\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. With the table open over the plot, the scene's markup, the figure's description, the plot's value text and the table are compared before and after three paused appends; after Resume the table holds every buffered row once, with its values.\",\n      \"area\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. With the table open over the plot, the scene's markup, the figure's description, the plot's value text and the table are compared before and after three paused appends; after Resume the table holds every buffered row once, with its values.\",\n      \"bar\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. With the table open over the plot, the scene's markup, the figure's description, the plot's value text and the table are compared before and after three paused appends; after Resume the table holds every buffered row once, with its values.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. With the table open over the plot, the scene's markup, the figure's description, the plot's value text and the table are compared before and after three paused appends; after Resume the table holds every buffered row once, with its values.\",\n      \"donut\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. With the table open over the plot, the scene's markup, the figure's description, the plot's value text and the table are compared before and after three paused appends; after Resume the table holds every buffered row once, with its values.\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"I5\",\n    \"statement\": \"First render is not animated. An update may transition for at most 200 ms. Under prefers-reduced-motion: reduce nothing transitions, on first render or on update.\",\n    \"appliesTo\": [\n      \"line\",\n      \"area\",\n      \"bar\",\n      \"scatter\",\n      \"donut\",\n      \"compact\"\n    ],\n    \"notApplicable\": {},\n    \"evidence\": {\n      \"line\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I5 line: first render is not animated (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference): from the first painted frame, frame by frame for 2.5 s, the marks' markup and computed paint never change and no animation runs on the chart; a screenshot taken with animations running matches the one at 2.5 s\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I5 line: first render is not animated (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce): from the first painted frame, frame by frame for 2.5 s, the marks' markup and computed paint never change and no animation runs on the chart; a screenshot taken with animations running matches the one at 2.5 s\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I5 line: an update shows the new data and settles within 200 ms of the call, on the page's clock; under reduced motion its first frame is already the final one, with no animation\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I5 line: a filter change across 24 charts on one page settles within 200 ms of the change, on the page's clock\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"area\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I5 area: first ren