rame, frame by frame for 1.5 s, the marks never change and no animation runs\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"browser\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/compact.browser.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"C2 compact bar: no motion (I5): from the first painted frame, frame by frame for 1.5 s, the marks never change and no animation runs\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"weak\": {\n      \"compact\": [\n        {\n          \"kind\": \"unit\",\n          \"file\": \"packages/axylo/test/acceptance/reader-model.test.ts\",\n          \"title\": \"I5 compact: the first model frame has final geometry and an update commits without intervening model frames\",\n          \"reason\": \"Node, for compact line, area and bar: the first frame draws once with the final model, and an update commits in one frame with none in between. Nothing is rendered or timed.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    \"gaps\": {\n      \"compact\": \"For compact area and bar, first render is traced only without a motion preference and for 1.5 s, and their updates are not traced in a browser; the 24-chart filter change runs on full charts only.\"\n    },\n    \"limits\": {\n      \"line\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Motion is traced on the page's clock: each frame's signature of the marks' markup and computed paint (traceMotion keeps only its length and last 120 characters when it is longer) and the animations running on the chart. The first frame is compared with the frames up to 2.5 s by that signature, not in pixels; the 0.1% pixel comparison is between the picture at about 2.5 s and 500 ms later. The 24-chart filter change uses 24 copies of the fixture, without a motion preference, on the machine that runs the suite.\",\n      \"area\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Motion is traced on the page's clock: each frame's signature of the marks' markup and computed paint (traceMotion keeps only its length and last 120 characters when it is longer) and the animations running on the chart. The first frame is compared with the frames up to 2.5 s by that signature, not in pixels; the 0.1% pixel comparison is between the picture at about 2.5 s and 500 ms later. The 24-chart filter change uses 24 copies of the fixture, without a motion preference, on the machine that runs the suite.\",\n      \"bar\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Motion is traced on the page's clock: each frame's signature of the marks' markup and computed paint (traceMotion keeps only its length and last 120 characters when it is longer) and the animations running on the chart. The first frame is compared with the frames up to 2.5 s by that signature, not in pixels; the 0.1% pixel comparison is between the picture at about 2.5 s and 500 ms later. The 24-chart filter change uses 24 copies of the fixture, without a motion preference, on the machine that runs the suite.\",\n      \"scatter\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Motion is traced on the page's clock: each frame's signature of the marks' markup and computed paint (traceMotion keeps only its length and last 120 characters when it is longer) and the animations running on the chart. The first frame is compared with the frames up to 2.5 s by that signature, not in pixels; the 0.1% pixel comparison is between the picture at about 2.5 s and 500 ms later. The 24-chart filter change uses 24 copies of the fixture, without a motion preference, on the machine that runs the suite.\",\n      \"donut\": \"Browser evidence: system Chrome, SVG renderer (the default); no Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet. Motion is traced on the page's clock: each frame's signature of the marks' markup and computed paint