{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_76","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git show d9fa4b0:reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/matrix-merge-notes/dx-p.md | rg -n 'P[1-8]|DX8|DX9|DX10|DX11|DX12' | tail -55\"","aggregated_output":"1:# Family dx-p: DX1–DX12, P1–P8\n39:- All six cells are now `pending`: the 1,000-cycle heap trend is P7's measurement (spec \"Verified by: … (P7)\"), and P7 is not measured.\n57:**DX8.** The statement follows the amended spec.\n61:  - `validate()`: `node.test.ts` dirty fixture for line, plus \"DX8 <type>\" in Node for every type.\n67:**DX9.** Was empty (no evidence). Now weak (`document`) `apps/docs/pages/stability.md` (the policy), plus `cannotVerify` on all types: no release exists (0.0.0), so there is no previous release, no API report and no release history.\n69:**DX10.**\n74:**DX11.**\n78:**DX12.** Was empty. Now `pending` on all types: the rehearsal has not been done (STATUS.md, next actions), and the repository holds no script, prompts or trap fixtures for it. It will be recorded as agent rehearsal, not as user evidence.\n80:**P1, P2, P3, P5.** Line only, with specific NA reasons: the plan's W-first \"create one line chart\", W-page \"24 × trend\", and the line-only P3 endpoints in `bench/src/decision.js`.\n84:**P4.** Line, area, bar and scatter (unchanged; donut and compact NA, reasons reworded). Each cell has `pending` with the owner's sentence. For area, bar and scatter it adds that the harness's hover workload draws a line.\n86:**P6.** Removed: the `scripts/size.mjs` document and the pending text. The evidence is now the same size entries as DX7: line gets `everything` and `line only`, the other types `everything`. The metric matches P6 (minified and gzipped, CSS inside the JavaScript). The limits match DX7's. Static status: **pass** from the record, which does not name its commit.\n88:**P7.** The statement gives the 1.1× budget.\n95:**P8.** Compact only (NA reasons rewritten: scatter and donut have no compact variant). `pending`: the owner's sentence. The P8 endpoint draws compact line tiles; compact area and bar have no workload.\n105:| DX5/line, area, bar, scatter, donut, compact | weak (gaps) | not run (pending) | The heap trend over 1,000 cycles is P7's measurement, not measured yet. Gaps remain for the non-line browser checks. |\n107:| DX8/line | evidence only, but refused (StrictMode, hydration, React) | evidence only (pass when run) | Current titles; every part cited. |\n108:| DX9/all | no evidence | cannot be verified here | No release exists to run an upgrade test or diff an API report against. |\n109:| DX10/line | weak | not run, permanently (checker) | Now cites the docs examples suite in full. Its per-example tests can only be cited by describe prefix, and the checker never passes that prefix (defect 1). |\n110:| DX10/area, bar, scatter, donut, compact | weak | not run, permanently (checker) | Same as line. |\n111:| DX11/all | evidence only, but refused (renamed titles) | evidence only (pass when run) | Current titles with ancestors. |\n112:| DX12/all | no evidence | not run (pending) | The rehearsal is pending work. |\n113:| P6/all | not run (pending) | pass (size record) | The size check measures P6's metric against the DX7 limit. |\n114:| P1, P2, P3, P5/line; P4; P7; P8 | not run | not run | Unchanged status. The benchmark weak citations were removed and the pending text reworded. |\n116:Every other cell keeps its status: DX1 area to donut weak; DX2 area, bar, scatter, compact weak and donut pass-capable; DX3, DX4 and DX6 weak; DX8 non-line weak.\n122:1. **DX10, all types.** The per-example render tests (`examples.browser.test.ts`, it.each over the example list) exist but cannot be counted: they can only be cited by describe prefix, and that prefix never passes (defect 1).\n123:2. **DX5, all types.** Heap trend over 1,000 create–destroy cycles is P7, not measured. For area, bar, scatter, donut and compact, nothing in a browser checks the one-turn sequence, the rejected strict update, or what `destroy()` releases (the element, listeners, observers, kept data); Node only.\n124:3. **DX8, area, bar, scatter, donut and compact.** Create, destroy and create again on one element, and \"leaks nothing\", are tested on line only. The missing-target error is checked through `line()` only.\n142:9. **P1, P2, P3, P5 (line), P4 (line, area, bar, scatter), P7 (all), P8 (compact).** Not measured. No benchmark workload exists for P4 on area, bar or scatter, for P7 on any non-line type, or for P8 on compact area or bar.\n143:10. **DX9 (no release) and DX12 (rehearsal not done), all types.**\n148:- **DX9** \"at most one major version a year\" and \"keeps working for at least … six months\": statements about release history. Not checkable until releases exist, and then only over time.\n149:- **DX11** \"verified at release\": the tests check the tarball `npm pack` makes now; \"at release\" is a process step.\n150:- **DX12** \"passes the reader criteria\": the agent's chart would have to be run through the whole reader suite (F, L, I, A). No script exists for that.\n151:- **DX5** \"releases everything\" and **DX8** \"leaks nothing\": unbounded. The tests check what a page can observe (DOM, listeners, observers, animation frames, WeakRef-collected data and figure).\n154:- **DX10** \"in CI\": `.github/workflows/ci.yml` lists the suites, but it has never run (no remote).\n156:- **P1** \"reference desktop\" and the \"named hardware profiles\": no profile is defined in a form a test could check.\n167:Negative controls (not cited): `csp.browser.test.ts` \"the instruments themselves\" → \"catch text inserted as HTML: the observer records the element, and each report names its directive and page\" covers `tests/dist/pages/observe.js` and the report URLs. DX8's CSP and text citations rely on that helper.\n171:1. **A describe prefix over tests with unexpandable `it.each` titles can never pass.** `titles.mjs` records `it.each(computed)('%s')` as a test with `title: null`. For a prefix citation, `resultFor` puts that null-title key in `expected`, and no result can match it. Confirmed with fabricated all-pass results: DX10 reads \"not run\" with the prefix and \"pass\" without it. Affected: `apps/docs/test/examples.browser.test.ts` (per-example renders), `diagnostics.test.ts`, `diagnostics.browser.test.ts` (\"each input does what its page says\"), `site.browser.test.ts`, `options.test.ts`. A `casePrefix` does not help either: it excludes the null key, but a passing result whose title is in neither `keys` nor a template is never added to `passed`. A fix could let a prefix citation declare `cases` for such suites, or exclude null-title registrations from `expected` when `cases` is given.\n172:2. **A title-only citation of a test inside `describe.each` with computed rows never passes.** The scanner cannot name the suite, so it records the test with ancestors `[]`. `expected` uses those static ancestors; results carry the real suite title. Confirmed: DX11 without `ancestors` reads \"not run\" with all-pass results. Affected: `tests/dist/licence.test.ts`, `snippets.test.ts`, `node.test.ts` (`%j` is not expanded either), `lifecycle.browser.test.ts`, `csp.browser.test.ts`, `text.browser.test.ts`, `flavours.browser.test.ts`, `isolation.test.ts`, `types.test.ts`. Workaround here: `ancestors` with the runtime suite titles, even where the title is in only one suite (licence: `[\"axylo\"]`). The brief says to give ancestors only when a title repeats; here the checker needs them.\n174:4. **Size citations have no provenance.** `resultFor` judges `bench/size-latest.json` as it is: the record names no commit, and the checker does not compare its tarball integrity with the current pack. P6 already reads \"pass\" statically. Recorded in the DX7 and P6 limits.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
