its label and unit only in the controller model (Node), and its field-name fallback is not checked; a time (instant) x and a category x are not checked, only a date x.\n- **L6** (area): pass when run → weak. Recorded reason: A measure (number) x on an area chart is titled with its label and unit only in the controller model (Node), and its field-name fallback is not checked; a time (instant) x and a category x are not checked, only a date x.\n- **L6** (bar): pass when run → weak. Recorded reason: A measure (number) x on a bar chart is titled with its label and unit only in the controller model (Node), and its field-name fallback is not checked; a date or time x on a bar chart is not checked, only a category x.\n- **L6** (scatter): pass when run → weak. Recorded reason: A time or date x on a scatter chart is not checked, only a number x.\n- **C1** (compact): pass when run → weak. Recorded reason: The name from labelledBy is read from Chrome's tree for compact line only; for compact area and bar only the model is checked. Pointer input is tried as a move to and a click at the centre of a tile; wheel, drag and touch on a compact chart are not tried in a browser (the model tests show only that the committed frame is not interactive and not zoomable).\n- **DX5** (line): weak → not run (pending). Recorded reason: Not measured yet: the heap trend over 1,000 create–destroy cycles is P7's measurement (spec DX5, \"Verified by\"); the benchmark harness in bench/ exists, and the acceptance measurements wait for a quiet machine (STATUS.md, 2026-11-18).\n- **DX5** (area, bar, scatter, donut, compact): weak → not run (pending). Recorded reason: In a browser, the one-turn sequence, the rejected strict update and what destroy() releases (the element, listeners, observers, kept data) are checked on line only (lifecycle.browser.test.ts); for this type they are checked only through the controller in Node.\n\n### Cells whose reachable status changed kind (neither up nor down) (5)\n\n- **A6** (line, area, bar, scatter, donut): cannot be verified here → not run (pending). Recorded reason: No Firefox or WebKit result is recorded yet: the criterion asks for the viewport and text-spacing tests in three engines.\n\n### Cells whose reachable status went up (39)\n\n- **F10** (compact): weak → pass when run. \n- **A5** (donut): weak → pass when run. \n- **I4** (line): cannot be verified here → weak. Recorded reason: Sizes: the table's pager and jump field are hidden on the fixtures' one-page tables, so they are not measured, and Resume is not measured. Touch: Pause and Resume, Pan, Reset, the table pager and the jump field are not shown to work by touch.\n- **I4** (area, scatter): cannot be verified here → weak. Recorded reason: Sizes: the table's pager and jump field are hidden on the fixtures' one-page tables, so they are not measured, and neither are Reset zoom, Pan left and Pan right (shown only while zoomed) or Resume. Touch: Select range, Pause and Resume, Pan, Reset, a pinned tooltip's rows, the table pager and the jump field are not shown to work by touch.\n- **I4** (bar): cannot be verified here → weak. Recorded reason: Sizes: the size test runs the category bar fixture, which has no zoom controls, so on number and date bars only the Select range toggle is measured; the table's pager and jump field are hidden on the fixtures' one-page tables, so they are not measured, and Resume is not measured. Touch: zoom on a number or date bar, Pause and Resume, a pinned tooltip's rows, the table pager and the jump field are not shown to work by touch.\n- **I4** (donut): cannot be verified here → weak. Recorded reason: Sizes: the table's pager and jump field are hidden on the fixtures' one-page tables, so they are not measured, and Resume is not measured. Touch: the slice list's entries, a pinned tooltip's row, Pause and Resume, the table pager and the jump field are not shown to work by touch.\n- **A9** (line, area, bar, scatter, donut, compact): no evidence → weak. Recorded reason: No test reads the generated page: that each listed criterion names the tests that cover it, that the page states what the author must supply and the limits of section 3.8 (both are hand-written in apps/docs/pages/conformance.md), or that uncited criteria are shown as not covered by a test. The list of WCAG 2.2 A and AA criteria is hand-written in apps/docs/data/wcag.mjs, and no test compares it with the W3C list. Publication with each release has no test.\n- **DX1** (compact): weak → not applicable. Recorded reason: A compact chart is a line, area or bar chart given compact: true (spec 3.7); it needs that option by definition, so the rule of data and fields only is about the full chart.\n- **DX2** (line): weak → pass when run. \n- **DX9** (line, area, bar, scatter, donut, compact): no evidence → cannot be verified here. Recorded reason: No release exists (the package is 0.0.0 and has never been published), so there is no previous release whose documented examples an upgrade test could compile and run, no API report to diff, and no release history to hold to the deprecation and major-version rules.\n- **DX10** (line, area, bar, scatter, donut, compact): weak → pass when run. \n- **DX12** (line, area, bar, scatter, donut, compact): no evidence → not run (pending). Recorded reason: Not done yet: the scripted agent rehearsal has not been run (STATUS.md, next actions, 2026-11-18), and the repository holds no script, prompts or trap fixtures for it. When it is run, it is recorded as agent rehearsal, not as user evidence.\n- **P6** (line, area, bar, scatter, donut, compact): not run (pending) → pass when run. \n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_83","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'git show d9fa4b0:reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/matrix-merge-notes/f-a.md'","aggregated_output":"# Family f-a: F1, F2, F4, F5, F7, F11, T-dense-line, T-dense-area, T-dense-bar, T-dense-donut, T-dense-scatter\n\nRows file: `.matrix-merge-scratch/rows/f-a.json` (11 rows, in matrix order). `node .matrix-merge-scratch/validate.mjs .matrix-merge-scratch/rows/f-a.json` prints `(checker: 0 problems in these rows; 99 in other rows, not shown)` and `OK: 11 rows, no problems found by this helper`. The checker throws on the other rows' problems, so the helper printed no per-cell statuses. I worked the statuses out by hand with `cellFor`'s order. \"not run\" below means evidence only and no gaps, which becomes pass once results are recorded.\n\nEvery cell that cites a browser test now has a `limits` text that starts with the required sentence. This replaces \"Browser acceptance evidence uses the SVG renderer in system Chrome.\"\n\n## Changes by criterion\n\n### F1\n- Statement: the current text. Bar and area value axes include zero. An author domain that excludes zero is widened to zero and raises AX110.\n- Applicability: unchanged (area, bar, compact). I made the not-applicable reasons specific: line and scatter are not under a rule for bar and area value axes, and a donut has no value axis.\n- Removed from area and bar, because the Node acceptance tests establish the same things through the controller (domain, AX110 and the baseline in the scene), per brief rule 5:\n  - `test/scale/domain.test.ts` \"with includeZero always contains zero, author domain or not\"\n  - `test/view/view.test.ts` \"widens area/bar author domains to zero and reports AX110\"\n  - `test/scene/scene.test.ts` \"uses a zero baseline for an unstacked area backed by a borrowed Float32 column\"\n  - `test/scene/scene.test.ts` \"uses projected zero as the baseline and represents missing and zero bars separately\"\n- Kept: the F1 property (1,000 runs over values from -100 to 100, with or without an excluding author domain) and the 82–97 fixture test, for area, bar, compact area and compact bar. Also the browser C2 compact area and bar test (value / 97 above the baseline).\n- Limits: Node scope. Only vertical bars are run; no horizontal bar chart is tested. Compact: the browser sentence; the AX110 case is Node only. A compact line is not under F1.\n\n### F2\n- Statement: the current text, with every part.\n- Kind corrected: \"F2 line: a generated absent daily step and the same explicit null produce the same gap\" uses `fc.assert`, so it is `property` (it was `unit`).\n- Citations otherwise unchanged. All of them were re-read; per-surface details are below.\n- Gaps added:\n  - line, area, bar: an absent step on a regular time (instant) axis is tested only at the data stage.\n  - scatter: no test asserts that an explicit null raises no diagnostic.\n  - donut: no test reads the tooltip of a null slice.\n  - compact: rewritten. Only compact line is drawn in Chrome. The generated-index property runs on compact area only. The time-axis gap applies here too.\n- Reader surfaces by type:\n  - line, area, bar: Chrome reads the tooltip's text, the table cells from the accessibility tree and the plot's value text. Node reads the tooltip model, the table model and `valueText`.\n  - scatter: the point is not drawn and the keyboard skips it (Chrome \"of 4\", Node walk). Only the table says \"No data\" (Chrome and Node).\n  - donut: the table says \"No data\" in Chrome and Node. The keyboard reading of null and absent slices is checked in Node only. The tooltip is not checked.\n  - compact: no tooltip, table or keyboard, so not applicable.\n\n### F4\n- Statement: the current text: three types, never mixed silently; zone in the tooltip heading and the description; AX111, AX112; a bare number is never an instant.\n- Kind corrected: \"F4 line: generated instants around DST and the year boundary preserve elapsed time and local readouts\" is `property` (it was `unit`).\n- Added for line: `test/browser/chart/data.browser.test.ts` \"the dates fixture as date strings gives identical tick text in UTC, America/Los_Angeles and Asia/Kolkata\". It is the only test that runs in real viewer zones (Playwright `timezoneId`). It covers calendar dates only.\n- Kept: the nine Node tests for each type (compact runs line, area and bar), plus \"A1 <type>: the summary of instants states the time zone they are shown in\".\n- Limits added:\n  - In Node, the viewer's zone is set by the test host, and the tooltip heading is read from the tooltip model.\n  - The A1 browser test uses an author `timeZone` (Asia/Kolkata), not the viewer's zone.\n  - Compact checks the zone in its description only.\n\n### F5\n- Statement: the current text, including the slot rule, cumulative sums and \"exact values come from the data\".\n- Not-applicable reasons now cite the section 3.6 cells: bar, a hint (AX132); scatter, a hint above 50,000 points; donut, no.\n- Citations: unchanged after re-reading.\n- Gaps added for area: no weekly-beside-daily test on area, and the one-in-a-million and alternating fixtures run on line only. Compact gaps rewritten: no slot-rule test, no browser test of a dense compact chart.\n- Limits:\n  - Node reads the kept samples per device-pixel column at DPR 1 and 2 and over three windows. Tied extremes come from the repeating generated backgrounds.\n  - Node's dense areas are always stacked.\n  - The browser check allows one device-pixel column either side, and does not show that the table row it reads (50,001) was dropped.\n\n### T-dense-line, T-dense-area, T-dense-bar, T-dense-donut, T-dense-scatter\n- Statements: unchanged; they match the section 3.6 cells word for word.\n- Not-applicable reasons reworded. The compact reason now points to section 3.7 (C2).\n- Citations: unchanged after re-reading.\n- T-dense-area gets the same gap as F5 area.\n- Limits added:\n  - bar: vertical bars on a category axis only; Chrome checks the hint's level, the count and the tall bar's place.\n  - donut: thin slices are checked by where their path starts.\n  - scatter: the count and six sampled points in Chrome; the threshold in Node.\n\n### F7\n- Statement: the amended text, with each part: precedence on value axes; x spans its data plus half a band; contents of the automatic domain; first tick; compact reference; percent/ratio; nothing from a label.\n- Kept: the F7 extents property and the percent/ratio tests (all five types), the reference-extreme property (line, area, bar, scatter) and F10 stack properties (area, bar).\n- Added:\n  - Node `type-matrix.test.ts` \"T-zoom-<type> <type>: numeric, time and calendar-date fields support zoom on x…\" (line, area, bar, scatter). It asserts that an author y domain [0, 10] is unchanged after an x zoom, the only test of the precedence rule on the y axis.\n  - Node \"T-reference-<type> <type>: a line and band extend the appropriate domains…\" (four types): a y line and an x band are contained.\n  - Browser \"T-reference-<type>: a reference line outside the data is included in the domain…\" (four types; reads the reported y domain), and for bar the band variant (a y band [150, 180]).\n  - `core/final-review.test.ts` \"a line on x 1.1 to 8.9 spans exactly its data (x is not a value axis)\" (line x span) and \"a scatter on x 1.1 to 8.9: the x domain ends at its first and last drawn ticks…\" (scatter x first tick).\n  - `view/view.test.ts` \"resolves references against the frame kind and includes value bands and lines in the domain\" (line, y band; view stage).\n  - `scene/scene.test.ts` \"centers whole continuous bars … (horizontal false)\" (x span [-0.5, 3.5]) and \"pads irregular bar endpoints by their own neighbour spacing…\" ([-1, 11.5]), for the half band on bars.\n  - Browser \"T-zoom-scatter: x only in 1.0…\" (with its `registration`): the automatic y domain is unchanged by an x zoom.\n  - Compact:\n    - `acceptance/compact.test.ts` \"C1 compact line: a reference has no effect on the domain or the description and is reported as not applicable\". It was uncited in coverage.txt; it runs compact line only.\n    - `diagnostics/registry.test.ts` \"AX150 reports the reference option once on compact area/bar\" (validation stage).\n    - F10 compact area and bar (stack totals).\n  - Weak: `layout.test.ts` \"for any automatic numeric x domain and any width…\" (scatter; 300 runs). `view.test.ts` \"keeps compact area/bar domains independent of references\" (100 runs, view stage).\n- Removed: none.\n- Gaps: all five cells. See the gap list.\n\n### F11\n- Statement: the current text.\n- Kind corrected: \"F11 scatter: generated unsorted and duplicate rows keep their x, y and caller row order\" is `property` (it was `unit`).\n- Citations: unchanged after re-reading.\n- Limits added:\n  - The Node scene uses a three-point shuffled fixture, not `trend`.\n  - For bar, only the duplicate-x rule applies (the ordering sentence names line, area and scatter).\n  - Compact: Chrome compares the SVG for all three kinds.\n\n## Cells whose status went down or up\n\nNone went up. \"Before\" is what the old fields could reach.\n\n| Cell | Before | Now | Reason |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| F2 line, area, bar | evidence only (pass once run) | weak | No chart test draws an absent step on a regular time (instant) axis. The spec names \"time or date\"; every drawn test uses a date axis. |\n| F2 scatter | evidence only | weak | Nothing asserts that an explicit null is silent on scatter: no codes are checked in the scatter gap tests. |\n| F2 donut | evidence only | weak | The tooltip of a null slice is never read. |\n| F2 compact | weak | weak | Gaps rewritten: compact area and bar are not drawn in Chrome; the property runs on compact area only; the time-axis gap. |\n| F5 area, T-dense-area | evidence only | weak | The weekly-beside-daily slot rule is never run on area. The one-in-a-million and alternating fixtures are line only. |\n| F5 compact | weak | weak | Gaps rewritten: no slot-rule test, no rendered dense compact chart. |\n| F7 line | evidence only | weak | Without an author domain, the y range after an x zoom is not shown to stay inside the automatic domain. The x span is tested on a numeric x only. |\n| F7 area | evidence only | weak | As line, plus: no test of an area's x span; nothing shows the domain ends at the first tick beyond the stack totals; no y band. |\n| F7 bar | evidence only | weak | As line, plus the stack-total tick. The half-band span is checked at the view stage on a numeric x. |\n| F7 scatter | evidence only | weak | The first-tick rule is tested on a number x only; a unit test asserts that a date x spans exactly its data. Percent/ratio is tested on y only. No y band. |\n| F7 compact | evidence only | weak | Compact area and bar: the reference's lack of effect is shown at the view stage only, the description is not checked, and AX150 only at validation. The first-tick check is skipped for compact layouts. No x-span test. |\n\nUnchanged, evidence only: all cells of F1, F4 and F11; F5 line; T-dense-line, T-dense-bar, T-dense-donut and T-dense-scatter.\n\n## No evidence (gap list), most important first\n\n1. **F7 line, area, bar**: without an author domain, the y range shown after an x zoom is never asserted to lie inside the automatic domain. The line view refits y to the visible data (view.test.ts), so the claim depends on that refit.\n2. **F7 scatter**: the first-tick ending on a date or time x. `view.test.ts` \"rounds numeric scatter x outward…\" asserts that a date x spans exactly its dates, and `core/axes.ts` applies the first-tick rule to a number x only. Either the spec or the implementation needs a word (see below).\n3. **F7 area**: no test that an area's continuous x spans exactly its data. Line has one (numeric). Bar has one at the view stage (numeric, regular and irregular steps). No test runs a time series on any of them.\n4. **F7 compact area and bar**: no controller-level test that a reference leaves the domain and the description unchanged. Only line has one. AX150 is checked at the validation stage only, and the view-stage property has 100 cases.\n5. **F2 line, area, bar, compact**: an absent step on a regular time (instant) axis, drawn. Only the data stage covers it (`test/data/review.test.ts` \"places a missing midnight in %s and reports AX111\"). Its tuple `it.each` title cannot be cited, because the scanner expands scalar lists only.\n6. **F2 compact area and bar**: nothing is drawn in Chrome: gaps, the isolated point, and the compact bar's \"no data\" mark. The Node scene is the only evidence.\n7. **F5 area (and T-dense-area)**: the weekly-beside-daily slot rule. The one-in-a-million outlier and the alternating valid and missing fixtures (line only).\n8. **F5 compact**: the slot rule; no browser test draws a dense compact chart.\n9. **F7 area, bar, compact**: nothing shows that the domain ends at the first tick at or beyond the stack totals (F10 asserts only that they are covered).\n10. **F7 compact**: whether the automatic domain ends at a tick (the helper skips compact layouts); a compact chart's x span.\n11. **F7 area, scatter**: a y reference band. Line has one at the view stage; bar has one in Chrome.\n12. **F7 scatter**: a declared percent or ratio scale on x.\n13. **F2 donut**: the tooltip of a null slice reached by keyboard.\n14. **F2 scatter**: that an explicit null raises no diagnostic.\n\nRecorded as limits, not gaps:\n- F4: only calendar dates (line ticks) are run in real browser viewer zones. Instants in the viewer's default zone are checked with the zone supplied by the Node host.\n- F1: no horizontal bar chart is run.\n- F11: line, area and scatter order is checked on the scene, not painted.\n\n## Not testable as written (or ambiguous)\n\n1. **F7, x span against reference containment.** The spec says that a continuous x of line, area or bar \"spans exactly its data\", and that the automatic domain contains \"the reference lines and bands the chart draws\". For an x reference beyond the data, the two conflict. The tests assert that the x domain reaches the reference:\n   - f-domains extents: `x.domain[1] >= 8`\n   - type-matrix T-reference: `x.domain[1] >= 6`\n   - view/review \"includes x lines and bands in the automatic extent\": [-3, 8] for line\n   I read \"its data\" as \"its data and x references, without tick padding\".\n2. **F7, a scatter's date or time x.** \"Both axes of scatter\" are value axes, but the first-tick rule is implemented and tested for a number x only, and a unit test asserts the opposite for dates. The spec should say whether a temporal x on scatter ends at a tick.\n3. **F7, \"the zoomed view\" on y.** Zoom changes x only in 1.0, so on line, area and bar the y \"zoomed view\" can only mean the y range after an x zoom. The spec does not say whether y refits. Line refits to the visible data (view.test.ts); scatter keeps the full y (browser T-zoom-scatter).\n4. **F7, compact \"ends at the first tick\".** A compact chart draws no ticks, so the rule has no visible meaning there. The tests do not assert it.\n5. **F5, slot rule in a stacked area.** \"A slot a series merely has no row for does not break its line\" may conflict with F10, \"a missing component is drawn with zero height and the stack is marked incomplete\". It is open whether a no-row slot in a stack is a missing component.\n6. **F2, scatter and donut readouts.** A scatter point without y has no position, and a null slice has no arc. Only the table (and, for donut, the keyboard) can say \"No data\". I treated the scatter tooltip and announcement as not reachable. I kept the donut tooltip as a gap, because the keyboard reaches the slice.\n\n## Titles that promise more than their assertions\n\n- `test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts:358`, \"T-dense-<type>: … each drawn in their own device-pixel column and nowhere else; … a sample the drawing dropped is in the table\":\n  - `spikeColumn` accepts a vertex within one device-pixel column either side, and reads SVG path vertices, not pixels.\n  - The table row read (50,001) is never shown to be one the drawing dropped.\n- `type-matrix.browser.test.ts:422`, \"T-dense-bar: … every bar is still drawn, each where its category is\": it asserts the count (2,000) and the place of the one tall bar only.\n- `type-matrix.browser.test.ts:580`, \"T-reference-<type>: a reference band outside the data is included in the domain…\", for line, area and scatter: the x band is only checked to lie right of the plot's middle. The x domain is not read, so a band drawn beyond the plot would pass. The bar band variant and every line variant do read the y domain.\n- `test/acceptance/f-domains.test.ts:64`, \"F7 <type>: for any generated extents the automatic domain includes data and references and the zoom stays inside its governing domain\":\n  - For compact, references are excluded by design and the first-tick check is skipped.\n  - For line, area and bar, the zoom checked is on x, which the amended F7 no longer places under the precedence rule.\n- `test/browser/acceptance/f2-gaps.browser.test.ts:104`, \"F2 <type>: with missing: 'zero' … drawn at zero, on the zero baseline\":\n  - For bar, it asserts only that no bar other than five is taller than 1.5 px. That a zero bar is drawn at days 2 and 4 is checked in Node.\n  - For compact line, it asserts that the two zeros are the lowest vertices, not where the baseline is.\n\n## Checker or helper defects\n\n- **Kind not checked.** The old matrix labelled three fast-check tests as `unit` (F2 line generated absent step, F4 line generated instants, F11 scatter generated rows). The checker does not compare `kind` with a test's use of fast-check, and it does not see run counts below the spec's 1,000:\n  - `view.test.ts` \"keeps compact %s domains independent of references\": fast-check's default of 100 runs.\n  - `layout.test.ts` scatter x property: 300 runs.\n- **`firstTicks` is silently vacuous for compact.** In `test/acceptance/f-domains.test.ts:53`, `firstTicks` returns without asserting when the layout kind is not `plot` (every compact chart) or the data is constant. Two F7 tests therefore assert nothing about ticks for compact.\n- **The spike-column control does not test the tolerance.** `checks.ts` `spikeColumn` tolerates ±1 device column. Its negative control (\"T-dense-line: negative control: the spike-column check reports a spike moved five columns away\") moves the spike five columns at DPR 1, so a one-column error is not shown to be caught.\n- **validate.mjs prints no statuses on errors.** It prints per-cell statuses only when the checker succeeds. With the 99 problems in other rows, it printed none, so I worked out the statuses by hand.\n- **Negative-control coverage of the helpers these rows rely on.**\n  - Covered: `spikeColumn` and `strokeRuns` (T-dense-line control), `readTable` and `compareTable` (A4 control), `valueText` (A2 control).\n  - Not covered by any control: the local `vertices` and `inkIn` in f2-gaps, the missing-bar patch comparison, `shapes`, `plotGeometry`, `ring`, `resolveColors`, compact `datumPoints` and the `__bench.describe()` domains.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_84","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'git show d9fa4b0:reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/matrix-merge-notes/i.md'","aggregated_output":"# Family i: I1–I6, T-pointer, T-tooltip, T-zoom\n\nRows: I1, T-pointer-{line,area,bar,donut,scatter}, T-tooltip-{line,area,bar,donut,scatter}, I2, I3, T-zoom-{line,area,bar,donut,scatter}, I4, I6, I5 (matrix order). Output: `.matrix-merge-scratch/rows/i.json`. Validation: `OK: 21 rows, no problems found by this helper` (the checker reports 0 problems in these rows and 99 in other rows). No test was run. The statuses below are static and worked out by hand from `cellFor`. The helper prints statuses only when the whole merged matrix passes the checker, which it did not, because of other rows.\n\nEvery browser cell's `limits` starts with the required sentence. No `engine`, `waivers`, `pending` or React or negative-control citation is used. Every title from the two acceptance directories was resolved from that directory's `EVIDENCE.json`. Titles from other files were resolved from the source. `registration` was added wherever the scanner holds the title only as a template.\n\n## Changes by criterion\n\n### I1\n- **Statement**: rewritten to the amended row. It covers the picking rule within one frame at p95, every visible series at the nearest x and \"No observation\" versus \"No data\" (line, area and bar), the viewport, the active mark, controls, hovering the tooltip, eight rows plus \"+N more\", readout mode at < 240 or < 140 px, no readout where the strip would leave the plot under L8's minimum, and Escape until a different datum.\n- **Applicability**: unchanged (all full types; compact not applicable, per 3.7 and C1).\n- **Removed**:\n  - The describe-wide prefix `I1 tooltip under the pointer` (with 9/9/9/7/6 cases). It is replaced by exact titles, one or more per part.\n  - Node `I1 {line,area,bar}: a pointer readout has eight rows, a remaining count and distinct missing text`. It is a model-level stand-in for rendered text, and the browser covers every part it touches. Its title also promises more than it asserts (see below).\n  - Node `I1 {scatter,donut}: picking a visible mark provides the same value as the keyboard tooltip model`. It only checks model-level picking.\n- **Added (evidence)**, per type:\n  - 20 positions\n  - can itself be hovered (it also asserts Escape until a different datum)\n  - never overlaps a control\n  - readout mode at the 240 px width limit and at the 140 px height limit\n  - ten series (line, area, bar, scatter)\n  - \"No observation\" (line, area, bar)\n  - `T-tooltip-<type>` browser test, for \"visible\" (line, area, bar)\n  - line only: final-closing `a legend button beside the plot with a 32 px outline…` (a control's painted outline)\n- **Added (weak, line)**:\n  - chart/scale `a strip two lines of 40 px text tall would leave the plot under 80 px…`\n  - final-hold `stepping the card's height…`\n  - core/final-review `boundary: exactly 80 px left beside the strip…`\n  - These three are the only tests near the L8-minimum case, and all of them run a line.\n- **Not cited, on purpose**: 12 of the uncited I1 titles in coverage.txt.\n  - `a hovered tooltip is text, not controls…` ×5 (pin mechanics, decision 0004 rule 4)\n  - `a hovered tooltip never stalls picking…` ×3 (rule 3)\n  - `rule 3b converse…` ×2 (bar)\n  - `a fast sweep that never rests…` ×2\n  - These test decision 0004's mechanics, not a part of the I1 criterion.\n- **Texts**:\n  - The old gaps (\"needs results from the decision 0004 revision 2 assertions\") described results. They are replaced by the parts not established.\n  - Limits now state how latency is counted, the 300 ms rest before hovering the tooltip, where the probes lie for scatter and donut, and how controls are taken.\n\n### T-pointer-*\n- Statements are the 3.6 cells. They are unchanged except for the separator wording.\n- **Removed**: lookup unit tests (`aligned.test.ts`, `donut.test.ts`, `scatter.test.ts`). The Node acceptance test and the browser test establish each cell's rule.\n- **Kept**: Node `type-matrix.test.ts` and browser `type-matrix.browser.test.ts` citations (bar: vertical and horizontal; scatter: radius and tie).\n- **Compact** reason made specific: no tooltip, no pointer-only behaviour.\n\n### T-tooltip-*\n- **line**: lookup `reads values, absent observations…` removed. Node and browser kept.\n- **area**:\n  - Statement is now \"Every visible series at that x, plus the stack total\" (3.6: \"Same, plus the stack total\").\n  - Node, browser (stacked) and the F10 area browser test are kept. The last one checks what the stack total reads for a mixed-sign stack.\n- **bar**:\n  - Statement is now \"Every series in that category\", which is the 3.6 cell. The old \"a mixed-sign stack gives both signed totals\" is not in the cell.\n  - The F10 bar citation is removed (it belongs to F10).\n- **donut**: lookup `picks the parts fixture…` removed (it is a picking test).\n- **scatter**:\n  - The lookup picking test is removed.\n  - The lookup `finds coincident points across a cell boundary…` test moved to `weak`, with a reason. It is the only test of grouping across the spatial index's cell boundary.\n\n### I2\n- **Statement**: the spec text.\n- **Applicability**: donut is kept not applicable after a re-check. The reason now says what the code does: a donut has one series, and its legend is F8's slice list, whose entries are `button.axylo-legend-choice` elements that select a slice, with no `aria-pressed` and `tabIndex = -1` (`src/dom/interaction.ts` `donutSliceList`). The reason also says the spec does not settle this (see \"Not testable as written\").\n- **Removed**:\n  - Node `I2 <type>: toggling a legend key removes that series…` ×4. These are model effects (marks, picking, table), not the button, its pressed state or the keys.\n  - chart/interaction `toggles by click, Enter and Space…` (line). It repeats the acceptance test.\n- **Kept**: acceptance `I2 <type>` ×4.\n\n### I3\n- **Statement**: the amended row (the four ways, the wheel rule).\n- **Applicability**: unchanged. Donut is not applicable (3.6 \"No\") and compact is not applicable (3.7).\n- **Removed**: Node `I3 <type>: touch is opt-in and disabling zoom hides controls…` ×4. They assert the model's `zoom` flag only. Opting in to touch is covered by the browser pinch tests.\n- **Added (line)**: five chart/interaction tests on the `trend` fixture (a time x): the buttons, the drag, the keyboard, the wheel and the pinch with `zoom: 'touch'`.\n- **Gaps (new)**: axis kinds no browser test exercises.\n  - line: date x, only `+`\n  - area: time x not at all, and date x only `+`\n  - bar: time x\n  - scatter: time and date x\n- **Limits**: which axis kinds and ways run, and that pinch goes through CDP touch events.\n\n### T-zoom-*\n- **Statements**: line, area and bar are \"On time, date and numeric x only (no category zoom in 1.0)\". Donut is \"No\". Scatter is \"Yes, both axes later; x only in 1.0\". The old scatter statement \"y keeps its full range\" is not in the spec, and `view.test.ts` shows the opposite at model level (see below).\n- **line**:\n  - Removed: chart/interaction `Zoom in and out are single clicks…`. It is now cited in I3.\n  - Added: `I3 line: from the keyboard…` (numeric x) and chart/interaction `keyboard: + and - zoom…` (time x).\n  - The category citations are kept.\n  - Gap: no user input on a category line is shown to leave the range alone.\n- **area**:\n  - Removed: `view/review.test.ts` `fits a monthly area between observations with the zero baseline`. It is about the y domain under zoom (F1/F7), not about which axes zoom.\n  - Added: `I3 area: from the keyboard…`.\n  - Gaps: time x only in Node, and category input as for line.\n- **bar**:\n  - Removed: snapshot `bar: zoom(['B','C'])…` and chart/interaction category. The T-zoom-bar browser test and the Node tests cover these, and do more.\n  - Gap: time x only in Node.\n- **donut**: unchanged citations. The limits now say that a drag and a pinch are not tried.\n- **scatter**:\n  - Removed: `view/view.test.ts` `keeps scatter ranges per series and uses only the points inside zoom for the value domain`. It asserts `yDomain` [2, 4] for the points inside the zoom. That is the y re-fitted to the visible points, which is F7 matter and contradicts the old statement.\n  - Added: `I3 scatter: from the keyboard…`.\n  - Gaps: \"x only\" is not asserted, and time and date x run only in Node.\n\n### I4\n- **Statement**: the amended row (Select range two-click addendum).\n- **Applicability**: unchanged. Compact is not applicable, and the reason now says that no test drags over a compact chart.\n- **cannotVerify removed** for every cell. The spec's own method is \"Touch emulation; size checks\", so a physical phone is not part of the criterion. The emulation is now in `limits`: taps through Playwright's touchscreen on a hasTouch page, the drag through CDP, and no physical device.\n- **Removed**: the describe-wide prefix `I4 single pointer, touch and target size`. It is replaced by exact titles.\n- **Added**:\n  - per type: the size test, the touch test, `I4 <type>: Select range…` (bar: number and date axis) and `I3 <type>: by single clicks only` (single-click zoom and pan)\n  - line also: a11y/axe `every control and the focus indicator are visible in forced colors…` (measures the zoomed, streaming toolbar: Pan left, Pan right, Reset zoom, Pause)\n  - line also: final-range `by touch: tap the toggle, then two taps on the plot`\n  - line also: review5 `tooltip rows pinned by a tap are buttons…`\n- **Gaps (new)**: per type, which controls are not measured and which interactions are not operated by touch (see the gap list).\n\n### I5\n- **Statement**: the spec text.\n- **Applicability**: all six types.\n- **Removed**: Node `I5 <type>` for full types (model frames only; the browser covers them).\n- **Kept (compact)**: Node `I5 compact` moved to `weak`, with a reason. It is model-level for compact line, area and bar.\n- **Added (compact)**: compact.browser `C2 compact {line,area,bar}: no motion (I5)…`.\n- **Compact gap text corrected**. The old text said that compact line, area and bar traces cover first render, but no such trace was cited, and the I5 compact tests trace a compact line only. The new gap: compact area and bar get first render only without a motion preference and for 1.5 s, and no browser update. The 24-chart change runs on full charts only.\n- **Limits**: state the surfaces, which are the per-frame markup and computed-paint signature, which may be truncated. The 0.1% pixel comparison is between about 2.5 s and 500 ms later, not first frame against 2.5 s.\n\n### I6\n- **Statement**: the spec text.\n- **Removed**:\n  - Node `I6 <type>` ×5 (model).\n  - chart/interaction `a pause control appears after append…` (line). It repeats the acceptance test.\n- **Kept**: acceptance `I6 <type>` ×5.\n- **Limits**: what the paused snapshot compares, with the table open over the plot.\n\n## Cells whose status went down or up\n\nStatic status, before (old fields) and now. \"Pass once run\" means evidence only, with no gaps; with no results for this commit it reads \"not run\".\n\n| Cell | Before | Now | Why |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| I1 line, area, bar, scatter, donut | weak | weak | Same status. The old gap described results. The new gap is the L8-minimum case (no readout, the datum highlighted); donut also has the whole-slice cover |\n| I3 line, area, bar, scatter | pass once run | **weak** | The time, date and numeric axis kinds are not all exercised for each type (see gaps) |\n| T-zoom-line, T-zoom-area | pass once run | **weak** | On a category x, only \"no controls\", \"no AX199 after +\" and the model's refusal of zoom() are asserted. Area also: time x only in Node |\n| T-zoom-bar | pass once run | **weak** | Time x only in Node |\n| T-zoom-scatter | pass once run | **weak** | \"x only\" is not asserted: the y check uses a window whose visible y extremes equal the full ones, and the zoom goes through the API. Time and date x run only in Node |\n| I4 line, area, bar, scatter, donut | cannot be verified here | **weak** | cannotVerify was dropped, because the spec's method is emulation. The cells are weak because the size test misses the pager, the jump field, Resume and the zoomed-only controls, and touch covers only some interactions |\n| I5 compact | weak | weak | Gap text corrected; C2 traces added; Node test moved to weak |\n| T-pointer ×5, T-tooltip ×5, I2 ×4, T-zoom-donut, I5 full ×5, I6 ×5 | pass once run | pass once run | Citations cleaned and texts rewritten; no change of status |\n\n## No evidence (gap list)\n\nMost important first. Each item is a criterion part, per chart type, that no test establishes.\n\n1. **I1, area, bar, scatter and donut: the plot whose strip would leave it under L8's 80 px.** In that case pointing must highlight the datum and show no readout. No test of any kind runs these types in that case. Line has partial support only: no strip and no floating tooltip (chart/scale), no floating tooltip and a hover event when under 140 px (final-hold), and the Node layout's 80 px boundary. No test asserts a visible highlight for any type.\n2. **I4, all types, sizes.**\n   - The table's pager and its jump field are never measured. The fixtures' tables have one page, so `pager.hidden = count <= 1` (`src/dom/table.ts`), and the size test skips hidden elements.\n   - Resume is never measured.\n   - Reset zoom, Pan left and Pan right (shown only while zoomed) are measured only on a line (a11y/axe, forced colours).\n   - Bar: the size test uses the category fixture, so on number and date bars only Select range is measured.\n3. **T-zoom-scatter**: that zoom changes x only, and no control or gesture zooms y.\n4. **I4, touch.** The tests tap the plot, the legend toggle, Zoom in and the table control. Reset and Hide table are tapped without any assertion. Not shown to work by touch, per type:\n   - line: Pause and Resume, Pan, Reset, the pager, the jump field\n   - area and scatter: also Select range and the pinned tooltip's rows\n   - bar: zoom on a number or date bar, Pause and Resume, pinned rows, the pager, the jump field\n   - donut: the slice list's entries, the pinned row, Pause and Resume, the pager, the jump field\n5. **T-zoom-line and T-zoom-area, category x**: that `+`, the wheel or a drag leaves the range unchanged in the browser. Only bar has this test.\n6. **I3, axis kinds**:\n   - line date x: only `+` is pressed\n   - area: time x not exercised; date x only `+`\n   - bar: time x not exercised\n   - scatter: time and date x not exercised\n7. **T-zoom-area, T-zoom-bar, T-zoom-scatter**: zoom on a time x, and on a date x for scatter, runs only through the Node controller's `zoom()`.\n8. **I5, compact area and bar**:\n   - no browser trace of an update\n   - first render under reduced motion not traced\n   - first render traced for 1.5 s, not 2.5 s\n   - the 24-chart filter change is not run on compact charts\n9. **I1 donut**: that the tooltip leaves the whole active slice uncovered. The 20-position test checks the 12 px square under the pointer only.\n10. **I1, all except line** (recorded as a limit, not a gap): a control's painted focus outline is checked only once, on a line (final-closing).\n\n## Not testable as written\n\n- **I2 and the donut.** I2 says \"Legend entries are toggle buttons\". F8 calls the donut's slice list \"the legend\". A2 places \"legend toggles\" in the toolbar, and a donut has one series, so there is nothing to toggle. The code makes the donut's entries buttons that select a slice, without a pressed state. As written, I2 either does not reach the donut (my reading, recorded as not applicable with that reason) or the donut cannot meet it. An owner question.\n- **I4, \"every interaction works … by touch\"** is an open set. A test can only sample it. The row would be checkable if it named the interactions: plot tap and pin, legend toggle, each toolbar control, Select range, pinned rows, table pager and jump field.\n- **I4, \"a one-finger drag on a chart scrolls the page\"** reads as if it reaches compact charts. Section 3.7 and C1 leave compact with no controls or pointer behaviour, so the row is recorded as not applicable to compact. No test drags over a compact chart.\n- **I5's method, \"first frame equals the frame at 2.5 s within a 0.1% pixel tolerance.\"** A harness cannot take a screenshot of the first painted frame at that frame, because screenshots are asynchronous. The suite compares each frame's markup and computed paint instead, plus pixels between about 2.5 s and 3 s.\n- **T-zoom-scatter, \"x only in 1.0\"** does not say what the y axis does when x is zoomed. F7 has value axes fit inside the automatic domain. `view.test.ts` shows y re-fitted to the points inside the zoom, while the browser test's title says \"the y axis keeps the full data range\". The spec should say which one holds.\n- **I1, \"highlights the datum\"** (below L8's minimum) does not say what counts as a highlight: a painted overlay, the focus ring, or only the `hover` event. The only test reads the event.\n- **I1's method, \"Hover at 20 positions including all four edges\"**, has nothing to show at the plot's edges for a donut, which picks nothing outside the ring, or for a sparse scatter. The test probes the ring and the points instead.\n\n## Titles that promise more than their assertions\n\n- `packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts:135`, `I1 ${type}: at 20 positions, the four edges included, … without covering the active mark`.\n  - Scatter: the probes are on and up to 12 px from five points, clamped 1 px inside the plot.\n  - Donut: the probes lie on the ring at 85% of the radius. Neither type is probed along the plot's edges.\n  - Donut: \"the active mark\" is checked as a 12 × 12 px square at the pointer, not the slice.\n- `i1-pointer.browser.test.ts:796`, `I4 ${type}: every control is at least 24 × 24 CSS px: toolbar, legend, table pager, jump field, …`.\n  - The pager and jump field are hidden on these one-page tables, and `measure` skips hidden elements, so they are never measured.\n  - Reset zoom, Pan left, Pan right and Resume are never shown during the test.\n  - The bar fixture has no zoom controls.\n- `i1-pointer.browser.test.ts:1012`, `I6 ${type}: … nothing a reader gets moves (marks, summary, value text, tooltip, open table) …`. The snapshot holds the scene, the description, the value text and the table. The tooltip is not compared, and with the table open the plot is inert, so no tooltip can show.\n- `i1-pointer.browser.test.ts:167`, `I1 ${type}: the tooltip can itself be hovered (decision 0004 revision 2, rule 3b)`. Rule 3b belongs to revision 3. This is cosmetic.\n- `packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts:275`, `T-zoom-scatter: x only in 1.0: + narrows the x range, controls are offered, and the y axis keeps the full data range though the visible y extremes change`.\n  - For scatter the test calls `charts[0].zoom([12, 22])`, not `+`.\n  - In [12, 22] the visible y values are 90–140, the same as the full range, as the test's own comment says. So \"the visible y extremes change\" is false for this fixture, and the y check cannot tell a kept range from a re-fitted one.\n- `packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/interaction.browser.test.ts:449`, `with zoom: 'touch' a pinch zooms through the public path; without it the chart leaves pinch to the page`. Only the `zoom: 'touch'` case runs. The default case's `touch-action: manipulation` is asserted in the previous test, and no pinch is sent without the option.\n- `interaction.browser.test.ts:58`, `at each of the four plot edges it stays inside the viewport and beside the active x`. \"Beside the active x\" is not asserted; the test asserts the viewport and that the box does not move. Not cited.\n- `interaction.browser.test.ts:138`, `a donut slice shows label, value and percentage; the overlay outlines it`. It asserts the label and \"46.2%\"; on this fixture the value and the share are the same text. The overlay is not checked. Not cited.\n- `packages/axylo/test/acceptance/reader-model.test.ts:230`, `I3 ${type}: touch is opt-in and disabling zoom hides controls`. It asserts the committed `zoom` flag. No control is looked at.\n- `reader-model.test.ts:267`, `I1 ${type}: a pointer readout has eight rows, a remaining count and distinct missing text`. It asserts eight rows, two more, and a \"No data\" row. \"No observation\" is not produced or checked, so nothing is shown to be distinct.\n- `packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/final-hold.browser.test.ts:388`, `… wherever the plot is shorter than 140 px, pointing shows the strip or no readout, never a floating tooltip, and still highlights`. Strip versus no readout is not asserted for any step, and \"highlights\" is the `hover` event, not something drawn. Cited as weak with that reason.\n\n## Checker or helper defects\n\n- **`traceMotion` truncates signatures** (`packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/checks.ts:177`). Signatures longer than 200 characters are returned as their length plus their last 120 characters. `settledAt` is computed on the full signatures, but the I5 first-render and reduced-motion assertions, and the C2 compact no-motion assertions, compare the truncated ones frame by frame. A change that keeps the length and lies outside the last 120 characters, such as a mid-markup coordinate of equal length, is not seen. The `animated` flag still catches CSS and Web animations, and the library has no animation code, so the risk is to the test's power, not a known miss. It is stated in the I5 limits.\n- **`validate.mjs` prints cell statuses only when the whole merged matrix passes the checker.** With problems in other families' rows it prints none, so the statuses here were derived by hand.\n- **Helpers my rows rely on that the negative controls cover**:\n  - `covered` (I1 bar: the occlusion check reports a tooltip moved over the active bars)\n  - `figureLayout` (I1 line: a strip that takes room only while a datum is shown)\n  - `traceMotion` (I5 line: an entry animation, and an update transition longer than 200 ms)\n- **Helpers with no negative control**: `inOrder`/`says` (tooltip text order), `cssSize` (I4) and `plotSides`/`plotTo` (readout limits).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_85","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'git show d9fa4b0:reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/matrix-merge-notes/f-b.md'","aggregated_output":"# Family f-b: F3, F12, F10, F8, F6, F9, T-limit-line, T-limit-area, T-limit-bar, T-limit-donut, T-limit-scatter\n\nRows file: `.matrix-merge-scratch/rows/f-b.json` (generated by a script in the worker's scratchpad that copies titles from the sources and EVIDENCE.json and adds `registration` only where the scanner cannot expand a title). Validation helper: `OK: 11 rows, no problems found by this helper`. Static statuses below are from the real checker, run on a copy of the matrix in which only these rows cite anything (the merged matrix fails on other rows still in progress, so the helper prints no statuses).\n\n## Changes by criterion\n\n### F3 (registry)\n- Statement: now states the registry's delivery rules (once per code per page in every build, hints in development only, strict throws from create/update/append, late findings never thrown, field and first rows in the caller's form) and the amended AX160 (value formatter shows the note, tick formatter does not) and AX199 (Axylo or author code it runs).\n- Applicability unchanged (all six).\n- Kept: every `dx-diagnostics.test.ts` registry case per type (each asserts level, one callback delivery, one console line in a development build, the message's fix, the internal effect, the drawn scene and the figure/table model), and production `F3 line: AX140 …`.\n- Added evidence, per type: DX2 (caller row indexes in row, column and wide forms), DX4 (field, row, chart name, delivered and printed once), both DX5 strict tests (warnings from create/update/append; an error from update); production `F12 <type>` (a warning printed once in a production build); `f-disclosure` three-bad-values (the dirty fixture yields exactly AX102, AX103, AX106); `F9 <type>` f-series (AX130's dash/marker/pattern differences, which the AX130 registry case does not assert); browser A1 AX140 in both builds (level, one console warning per page, generated name in Chrome's tree); browser L8 width and height (AX142 level and the fallback); browser F12 dirty (production) and F12 throwing readout formatter (production: AX160 with the note); browser T-limit (AX130 level, painted cues). Type-specific: line DX4 two-charts-one-page and production hint AX104; `F2 line/area/compact` AX105 browser; T-dense-bar (AX132), T-dense-scatter (AX133); donut F8 AX120 and AX121 browser and F12 AX121 note; compact C1 AX140 (three kinds, both builds), C2 dirty (three kinds), C4 AX131 (three kinds), C5 production; line browser chart tests for AX199 (interaction), tick-formatter AX160 fallback under strict (data) and no note (review).\n- Moved: A5 `… AX141 is raised` from evidence to weak (it asserts only that the code appears after the page changes the background).\n- Removed: `tests/dist/node.test.ts` validate() citations from area, bar, scatter, donut and compact (the probe validates a line chart only); kept as weak on line, with ancestors for its two `describe.each` suites.\n- Added weak: final-review `<kind>: an unknown option and a throwing x getter: AX150 then AX199` (line, area, bar, scatter: author-code AX199, code only); L7 internal-failure state in Chrome (all types, code not asserted); delivery module unit tests (once per page in production; hints only in development); round3 scatter tick formatter AX160.\n- Gaps rewritten per type to name the codes and delivery rules without a per-type check (see the gap list). Old gap text was generic. Limits: the required browser sentence plus the scope of the Node acceptance evidence (scene and models, development build unless named), and for compact which kinds each suite runs.\n- Applicability judgements used for the gap texts (the registry names no chart types): AX105 does not reach scatter (no gaps on a point chart) or donut; AX107, AX109, AX111, AX112, AX151 and AX152 do not reach donut; AX108 does not reach scatter (F11); AX110 reaches area, bar and compact area/bar; AX134 reaches line, area, bar and compact; AX142 and AX143 do not reach compact (no plot fallback, no labels); AX132 reaches compact bar.\n\n### F12\n- Statement amended to the current wording (example count 2, \"worded so it reads correctly for any count\").\n- Compact N/A reason made specific: corner marker with text equivalent and the description (C5).\n- Removed (line): the two `tests/dist/text.browser.test.ts` citations; they test message overrides (the brief says that fixture is being changed), and the acceptance F12 tests cover the line note in both builds.\n- Kept all acceptance citations (browser dirty in both builds, count of one, throwing readout formatter in both builds, donut AX121; Node three-bad-values, throwing formatter, production).\n- Added gap (line, area, bar, scatter): no test checks the note for AX107. Limits: the browser sentence, that the changed-values tests replace the note's text through messages, and that the count-of-one case is development only.\n\n### F10\n- Statement amended (readout total rule: sum when signs agree, positive and negative totals when mixed, not the net).\n- Area: removed `lookup/aligned.test.ts` \"uses the author's mixed total format…\" (a bar-frame unit test); added Node `T-tooltip-area area: …` (tooltip total \"6 (incomplete)\") and browser `T-tooltip-area: …` (same-sign total is the sum in Chrome's tooltip).\n- Bar: kept; dropped the unneeded `ancestors`; added a gap: no test checks that a stacked bar's tooltip marks an incomplete stack (the Node test checks the table row and the value text; its tooltip check is only the row values).\n- Compact: removed the old gap (it described an archive result, not a missing check). Limits say which kinds run (area, bar) and that the summary carries \"incomplete\" because a compact chart has no tooltip, table or announcements.\n- Donut N/A reason reworded.\n\n### F8\n- Statement amended to the full current criterion (legend text, zero/null listing, AX120 error state, grouping only positive slices, table lists every category, all-zero empty state).\n- Fixed: the three `format/index.test.ts` citations were `kind: \"browser\"`; they are Node unit tests. Kept two (share rounding); removed \"a ratio-scaled value keeps the readout digits of F6\" (an F6 matter, not a share rule). Dropped unneeded `ancestors`.\n- Added: browser chart `a donut with more than eight slices lists \"Other\" with its count, and a zero slice without an arc` (rendered: a zero slice stays on its own while grouping happens; table lists all ten); Node `F6 donut: percentage text is independently localized in tooltip and table` (one fraction digit on reader surfaces).\n- Added gap: a null slice is never checked while grouping happens. Limits: rendered legend shares are whole numbers; rounding is checked on the formatter and the Node models.\n\n### F6\n- Statement amended to the current criterion (six significant digits, leading zeros of the fraction not counted, unit).\n- Line: kept the Node tests and review5 (page `lang` change re-formats the summary in Chrome); added browser data `a custom formatter that throws falls back …` (tick formatter fallback on drawn ticks, AX160, not thrown under strict); weak review2 (focused text in de-DE, from the locale option).\n- All types: added weak formatter unit tests (default ticks in de-DE/en-IN, percent and ratio readouts, zoned times in three locales, tick formatter fallback) where only they check that part.\n- Gaps rewritten per type to name what is missing (page locale outside line, localized default ticks, percent readouts, zoned times, tick-formatter fallback on area/bar/scatter, en-IN shares). Old gaps were generic (\"do not compare all localized reader surfaces\"). Limits added (Node models; compact reads only its description; compact kinds line, area, bar).\n\n### F9\n- Statement amended (32 distinct combinations for every chart type; bars full and compact use fill pattern).\n- Donut N/A reason made specific (slices, at most eight arcs, F8).\n- Line and area: no citation removed; added gaps: no citable test reaches 32 series (see checker defects: the scene module's 32-combination cases cannot be cited). Scatter: added `scene.test.ts` `scatter` (32 distinct combinations on the scene). Compact: added `F3 compact: AX130 …` (all kinds), rewrote the gap.\n- Limits per cell say what is painted (8 and 9 series; bar 32) and what is checked on scene marks.\n\n### T-limit-line, -area, -bar, -scatter\n- Statement: \"Eight series: more than eight series raise AX130 (section 3.6)\". Compact N/A reason made specific (no compact column; C4/AX131).\n- Line: removed `core/controller.test.ts` \"a ninth series is rejected (AX130)…\" (a strict-append rejection, a DX5/strict matter) and `view/view.test.ts` 12-series unit test (covered by the acceptance f-series test).\n- All four: added `F3 <type>: AX130 …` (level and delivery of AX130).\n\n### T-limit-donut\n- Statement: \"Eight slices: more than eight slices with an arc raise AX121; zero and null slices do not count (section 3.6, F8)\".\n- Removed the two `view/view.test.ts` unit tests (tie-break order and partially negative ring are not this cell); added `F3 donut: AX121 …` (level, delivery).\n\n## Cells whose status went down or up\n\nStatic status before (old fields) → now:\n- F12 line, area, bar, scatter: pass-able (not run, no gaps) → weak. The AX107 omission is a warning that leaves a value out; no test checks its note.\n- F10 bar: pass-able → weak. The stacked bar tooltip's \"incomplete\" mark is not asserted anywhere.\n- F10 compact: weak → pass-able. The old gap described a missing archive result, not a missing check; the Node tests cover both compact kinds that stack.\n- F8 donut: pass-able → weak. \"Never grouped\" is not checked for a null slice when grouping happens.\n- F9 line, area: pass-able → weak. The only 32-combination check for them cannot be cited, and the cited tests reach 24 (line) and 12 (area) series.\n- Unchanged: F3 all weak; F6 all weak; F9 bar and scatter pass-able, compact weak; F12 donut pass-able; F10 area pass-able; all T-limit cells pass-able. (Pass-able cells read \"not run\" until results are recorded.)\n\n## No evidence (gap list)\n\nMost important first.\n1. F3, all types: delivery rules without a per-type check. Errors printing in a production build (no chart test; only the delivery module's unit test). Two charts on one page printing a code once (line, development build only; production only in the unit test). Hints silent in a production build (line only). Under strict: an error found on create or append (an acceptance test checks update per type; on line, unit tests check create and append without naming the code), a hint not throwing (no chart test), and late findings other than AX160 (and AX141 on line) not throwing.\n2. F3, area, bar, scatter, donut, compact: AX199 has no check of level, delivery and error state; only the code from a throwing x getter (unit, line/area/bar/scatter) and the internal-failure state without its code (L7 in Chrome). On line, AX199 from author code is checked only as the code.\n3. F3, all types except line: AX141 is only seen as raised in Chrome after the background changes (compact: line kind only); no level, delivery or drawing check.\n4. F9 line, area, compact: 32 distinct combinations not established by a citable test.\n5. F10 bar: tooltip \"incomplete\" for an incomplete stack.\n6. F8 donut: a null slice when grouping happens.\n7. F12 line, area, bar, scatter: the note for AX107.\n8. F6: page locale in a browser on area, bar, scatter, donut, compact; default tick text in de-DE and en-IN on a chart (formatter only); percent- and ratio-scaled readouts on a chart (formatter only); zoned times on a chart in en-IN (line) and in any non-en-US locale on area, bar, scatter, compact (formatter only); a throwing tick formatter's fallback on area and bar (formatter only) and scatter (code only); donut percentages in en-IN.\n9. F9 compact: painted colours for compact area and bar; any painted check beyond eight series for any compact kind.\n10. F3 smaller codes: AX143 on line and area (message wording only, unit) and scatter (none); AX132 on compact bar; AX142 delivery on area, bar, scatter, donut (Chrome checks level and fallback); a throwing tick formatter (AX160 without a note) on area, bar and scatter; the AX107 note on line, area, bar, scatter (summary count only).\n11. F3: field and first row indexes per type only for AX102, AX103, AX106 (line also AX104); other data codes only in registry unit tests on line data; the cap at the first ten rows only in a collector unit test.\n\n## Not testable as written\n\n- F9 \"after which combinations repeat\": describes what is allowed after 32; a test could only pin the implementation's chosen cycle.\n- F12 \"worded so it reads correctly for any count\": a language judgement. Tests check the exact text for 1 and 3 (and the template).\n- F6 \"ticks may be compact (50K)\": permissive. Checked with an author compact tick format (Node) and the default compact form at a million or more (formatter unit test).\n- Spec 3.5 \"Warning: … the reader sees the note in F12\" against F12's narrower \"values left out or changed\": AX110, AX130, AX140, AX141, AX150, AX151, AX152 are warnings with no note. The tests follow F12 (AX140 and AX150 assert no note; a tick formatter's AX160 asserts no note). The registry rows should say which warnings carry the note.\n- F10 for compact: \"tooltip, table and announcements\" do not exist on a compact chart; the test reads it as the summary (its title says so).\n- F6 \"page locale\": the Node suite takes the locale from a host stub; only a browser test can show it comes from the page.\n- The registry names no chart types per code; the applicability judgements listed under F3 are inferred.\n\n## Titles that promise more than their assertions\n\n- `packages/axylo/test/acceptance/dx-diagnostics.test.ts:155`, \"F3 <type>: AX130 keeps all nine series and assigns a secondary cue\": asserts the summary says \"9 series\" and nine marks; no secondary cue is asserted (f-series does that, so F3 cites both).\n- `packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/f8-donut.browser.test.ts:140`, \"F8 donut: eight slices are all drawn and raise no AX121; the ninth is what groups\": no ninth slice is added; only eight slices without AX121 are checked.\n- `packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/type-matrix.browser.test.ts:248`, \"F10 area: … and the parts sit on their own sides of zero\": the sides are asserted only `if (type === 'bar')`; for area only the tooltip total is asserted. F10 area relies on the property test for sides.\n- `packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-disclosure.test.ts:42`, \"F12 <type>: a throwing formatter discloses changed presentation even though the value is still drawn\": asserts AX160, the note, the summary and the table text; nothing about the drawn marks.\n- `packages/axylo/test/acceptance/f-series.test.ts:6`, \"F9 <type>: … twelve retain distinct painted cues …\": a Node test; it asserts the scene marks' paint bindings with dash, marker or pattern, not painted pixels.\n- `packages/axylo/test/core/closing.test.ts:49` (describe at 48, \"a tick formatter's AX160 does not change the fit\"): the test never asserts that AX160 is raised; it asserts the layout settles and no note.\n- Not a false promise but not citable for AX143: `packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/l-legibility.browser.test.ts:156` \"L1 bar: … or the note says labels are hidden and AX143 is raised\" asserts AX143 only if the note appears.\n\n## Checker or helper defects\n\n- `acceptance/titles.mjs` cannot expand `it.each(cases)` when `cases` is a variable (`packages/axylo/test/scene/scene.test.ts:731`, the F9 32-combination cases for line, area and bar, full and compact). The cases register with no title, so a describe-prefix citation can never pass (by design) and no exact title exists. Writing the list inline would make the test citable and lift F9 line and area.\n- The checker does not check `kind` against the file: the old F8 row cited Node unit tests in `format/index.test.ts` as `browser`, which would wait for a Chrome result that a Node run never gives.\n- The F3 registry rule only collects `AX\\d+` from cited titles, so a title that names a code satisfies it whatever the test asserts (example: the AX130 case above).\n- `validate.mjs` prints cell statuses only when the whole merged matrix has no structural error; while other families are in progress it prints none. Statuses here come from the real checker on a copy where only these rows cite tests.\n- Negative controls these rows depend on: painted-colour sampling (`paintedSeries`/`inkColor`, A5 line control) for the A5 palette and AX141 citations and the C4 compact bar texture. No negative control covers the helpers behind T-limit (`cues()`), F8 (`ring`/pixel sampling at mid angles), F12 (`noteState`), F10 (bar sides from `shapes`) or L8 (`plotDrawn`).\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
