{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_140","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git grep -n -i -e 'rehearsal' d9fa4b0 -- STATUS.md | tail -6\"","aggregated_output":"d9fa4b0:STATUS.md:21:| M4 Accessibility | In progress (chart core part 2). Screen-reader rehearsal cannot be done here |\nd9fa4b0:STATUS.md:62:Owner decisions on 2026-11-18: palette candidate B adopted (9861f54); size targets 96 KiB everything and 80 KiB line only (spec DX7); licence stays MIT with holder \"The Axylo authors\"; Playwright browser downloads allowed; no screen-reader rehearsal for 1.0 (state it as not done, do not block on it); the React adapter is removed from 1.0 (bf93e1a); Anthropic models build and fix, Codex reviews; memory budget P7 is 1.1× the caller's two columns (4a1db68); review rounds on the controller and interaction layers stop after round 3 with one last narrow check, leftovers become documented limits. Size targets for 1.0 raised to 116 KiB everything and 98 KiB line only (63c5b65, \"Raise targets\"); streaming as an opt-in import, worth about 15 KiB, is the first size item after 1.0.\nd9fa4b0:STATUS.md:75:- The acceptance matrix is stale: React rows, new and renamed tests, engines, DX1/DX7/DX8, the P7 bound, A3 rehearsal not done by the owner's decision.\nd9fa4b0:STATUS.md:88:8. Agent rehearsal (DX12); Phase 1 comparison rerun with Axylo included.\nd9fa4b0:STATUS.md:97:- **Still outside this machine:** Safari on macOS and iOS, a real phone, Windows. No screen-reader rehearsal will be done for 1.0 (owner's decision); the docs and the conformance table say so.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
