{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_141","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'git show d9fa4b0:packages/axylo/src/scene/lines.ts'","aggregated_output":"import {\n  SLOT_VALUE, type AlignedView, type IndexRange, type PathMark, type PointMark, type Projection,\n  type Rect, type ScatterView, type SeriesCue,\n} from '../core/contracts';\nimport { buildPath, buildPoints, simplifyLine, type JoinedRuns, type LineInput } from '../simplify';\nimport { position, seriesPaint } from './geometry';\n\nexport type XY = Extract<Projection, { kind: 'xy' }>;\nexport type Drawing = Omit<LineInput, 'y' | 'slot' | 'range'> & {\n  readonly mapX: (x: number) => number;\n  readonly mapY: (y: number) => number;\n};\n\nexport function drawing(x: Float64Array, xy: XY, plot: Rect, devicePixelRatio: number): Drawing {\n  return {\n    x, mapX: value => position(xy.x, value), mapY: value => position(xy.y, value),\n    left: plot.x, width: plot.width, devicePixelRatio,\n  };\n}\n\nfunction markerIndexes(\n  input: LineInput & Drawing, range: IndexRange, isolated: Uint32Array, compact: boolean,\n): Uint32Array {\n  if (compact) return isolated;\n  const { slot, x, mapX } = input;\n  let count = 0;\n  let first = range.end;\n  let last = range.start;\n  let previousPixel = 0;\n  let showAll = true;\n  for (let i = range.start; i < range.end; i++) {\n    if (slot[i] !== SLOT_VALUE) continue;\n    if (count++ === 0) first = i;\n    if (showAll) {\n      const pixel = mapX(x[i]!);\n      showAll = i === first || Math.abs(pixel - previousPixel) >= 12;\n      previousPixel = pixel;\n    }\n    last = i;\n  }\n  if (!count) return isolated;\n  const span = Math.abs(mapX(x[last]!) - mapX(x[first]!));\n  const capacity = showAll ? count : Math.min(count, Math.floor(span / 80) + 1 + isolated.length);\n  const indexes = new Uint32Array(capacity);\n  let write = capacity;\n  let previous = Infinity;\n  let single = isolated.length - 1;\n  // Walk back from the last observed value so the series always has its identity at that end.\n  for (let i = last; i >= first; i--) {\n    if (slot[i] !== SLOT_VALUE) continue;\n    const pixel = mapX(x[i]!);\n    const required = isolated[single] === i;\n    if (required) single--;\n    if (showAll || required || Math.abs(previous - pixel) >= 80) {\n      indexes[--write] = i;\n      previous = pixel;\n    }\n  }\n  return indexes.subarray(write);\n}\n\nfunction pointMark(series: number, cue: SeriesCue, xy: Float32Array): PointMark {\n  return { type: 'points', series, xy, shape: cue.marker, size: 6, fill: seriesPaint(series) };\n}\n\nexport function addLine(\n  input: LineInput & Drawing, view: AlignedView, series: number, visible: IndexRange, compact: boolean,\n  paths: PathMark[], points: PointMark[], selection: JoinedRuns = simplifyLine(input),\n): void {\n  const cue = view.cues[series]!;\n  // A single slot in an author domain can have joined neighbours outside the drawing.\n  const singlePoint = input.range.end - input.range.start === 1 && selection.indexes.length === 1;\n  if (selection.indexes.length && !singlePoint) {\n    paths.push({\n      type: 'path', series, xy: buildPath(selection.indexes, selection.breaks, input), stroke: seriesPaint(series),\n      strokeWidth: 2, dash: cue.dash,\n    });\n  }\n  const markers = markerIndexes(input, visible, singlePoint ? selection.indexes : selection.isolated, compact);\n  if (markers.length) points.push(pointMark(series, cue, buildPoints(markers, input)));\n}\n\nexport function scatterPoints(view: ScatterView, projection: XY): PointMark[] {\n  const result: PointMark[] = [];\n  for (let i = 0; i < view.frame.series.length; i++) {\n    if (!view.visible[i]) continue;\n    const { x, y } = view.frame.series[i]!;\n    const { start, end } = view.visiblePoints[i]!;\n    const xy = new Float32Array(2 * (end - start));\n    for (let index = start, out = 0; index < end; index++) {\n      xy[out++] = position(projection.x, x[index]!);\n      xy[out++] = position(projection.y, y[index]!);\n    }\n    result.push(pointMark(i, view.cues[i]!, xy));\n  }\n  return result;\n}\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_142","type":"agent_message","text":"## 1. Cells that could be reported as passing\n\n**The 117 figure counts cells with no blocking field. It overstates both checker reachability and evidentiary coverage.** Six DX10 cells cannot reach `pass` with their current citations. Six P6 cells already say `pass` from a size record last changed in `0167eda`, before ten library source files changed. That leaves **at most 105 cells that could newly pass on test results**, before judging what those tests assert.\n\nI reviewed **82 of the 117 cells** at `d9fa4b0`, including all 43 requested cells and 39 additional cells. My verdicts are **24 established, 52 weak, and 6 not established for this revision**. “Established” means that passing the cited assertions would establish the applicable statement. It is not a test result.\n\nAll line numbers refer to the commit. `B/` means `packages/axylo/test/browser/acceptance/`, `N/` means `packages/axylo/test/acceptance/`, `H/` means `packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/`, and `D/` means `tests/dist/`. **Full** means line, area, bar, scatter and donut. **All six** also includes compact. In a `T-…-*` row, each listed type identifies its own matrix row and cell.\n\n| Row | Type | Verdict | What the citations establish or miss |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| F1 | area | Established | The property checks the domain, exact widening, AX110 and the drawn zero baseline for signed data. `N/f-domains.test.ts:10–34` |\n| F1 | bar, compact | Weak | The bar assertions measure vertical edges only. Horizontal bars are a supported option, including with `compact`. Compact area is covered. `N/f-domains.test.ts:12–32`, `B/compact.browser.test.ts:97–109`, `packages/axylo/src/public.ts:121` |\n| F4 | line, area, bar, scatter, compact | Weak | Dates, instant forms, default and explicit zones, wall times, DST and diagnostics have substantive checks. The sole mixed fixture has a calendar majority. A parser that silently combines wall times and instants when there are no calendar dates passes it. `N/f-time.test.ts:61–100,137–147` |\n| F11 | line, area, bar, scatter, compact | Established | The tests compare coordinates and caller-row identities to the shuffled input, isolate AX108 to the affected series, and preserve coincident scatter rows. All three compact kinds are exercised. `N/f-order.test.ts:5–26,37–52,59–82` |\n| I2 | line, area, bar, scatter | Weak | Click, Enter, Space, computed pressed state and disappearing marks are all checked for the **first** legend entry. Every other entry could be inert, or toggling the first could hide both series. `B/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts:534–552` |\n| I6 | full | Weak | Pause buffers three appends and Resume restores the expected rows. The sole frozen-view comparison happens with the table open and the plot inert. It never compares a visible tooltip or the ordinary, table-closed view. `B/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts:1016–1040` |\n| A1 | full | Weak | Names, heading levels, summary clauses, AX140 and initial IDs have direct checks. A fully visible heading with `clip-path: inset(0)` satisfies the hidden-title assertion. The 24-chart ID check also precedes opening any tables. `B/a1-names.browser.test.ts:79–100,144–161` |\n| A4 | line | Weak | Paging, range restriction, layout stability and the jump to row 900,123 are checked. `123.25` is the only asserted fractional value. The F6 precision and locale rules remain open. In Chrome the helper accepts any computed table name as the caption. The region check measures height and focusability without scrolling it. `B/a4-table.browser.test.ts:27–55,203–217`, `B/util.ts:621–634` |\n| A7 | full | Weak | The 24-stream test and retained-datum checks cover real behavior. The observer misses text changes inside an existing implicit `role=\"log\"`. The focused test compares snapshots after two appends, which can miss an intervening rewrite. Donut strips share and position before comparison. A7’s citations do not exercise an L7 state announcement. `B/a6-a10.browser.test.ts:94–115,150–173` |\n| L5 | line, area | Weak | The fixtures bracket 12 px closely and exercise an isolated point. All threshold fixtures have uniform spacing. An implementation using average spacing would pass on a series with one pair closer than 12 px. Equality at 12 is also untested. `B/l-legibility.browser.test.ts:507–543`, `N/reader-model.test.ts:299–313` |\n| C3 | compact | Weak | All three kinds fill the three stated test sizes and default to 32 px. Every explicit resize increases width and height together. Independent sizing, such as a wide 16 px-high tile, remains open. `B/compact.browser.test.ts:179–198`, `N/compact.test.ts:78–91` |\n| DX8 | line | Weak | Packed Node import and validation, a real CSP header, the selector error and observable teardown have direct checks. The retention test weakly references only the outer rows array and figure. Retained row objects or internal buffers escape it. Reference labels are absent from the text-source fixture. `H/lifecycle.browser.test.ts:349–363`, `D/pages/sentinels.ts:12–42`, `D/csp.browser.test.ts:110–118,197–204` |\n| DX11 | all six | Weak | The packed MIT declaration, licence text, inventory and recognizable headers are checked. The source audit rebuilds one entry. The origin check for shipped JS verifies a directory name and suffix, without tying the shipped bytes to that build. Verification at release also remains outstanding. `D/licence.test.ts:28–33,57–75,95–116,128–130`, `.github/workflows/ci.yml:6–9` |\n| T-pointer-* | line, area, bar, donut | Established | Probes discriminate neighboring x values, bar bands in both orientations, and individual slices, the hole and the outside of the ring. `N/type-matrix.test.ts:34–48,96–105`, `B/type-matrix.browser.test.ts:29–92` |\n| T-pointer-scatter | scatter | Weak | The tests discriminate the radius and reverse the winner of an exact tie. They never require the closer **of two eligible points at unequal distances** to win. `N/type-matrix.test.ts:115–121`, `B/type-matrix.browser.test.ts:94–122` |\n| T-tooltip-* | line, bar, scatter, donut | Established | Fixture-derived labels and values, hidden series, both bar orientations, the donut share, and the eight-of-ten coincident scatter readout are checked where applicable. I used I1’s eight-row cap when reading “every visible series.” `N/type-matrix.test.ts:53–71,124–145`, `B/type-matrix.browser.test.ts:142–199` |\n| T-tooltip-area | area | Weak | The initial total, mixed signed totals and hidden-series exclusion are checked. After a series is hidden, a stale total still passes. `B/type-matrix.browser.test.ts:143–155,259–265` |\n| T-reference-* | line, area, bar, scatter | Established | Together the model and browser establish line and band support. For the stronger line row the model checks numeric domain inclusion, coordinates and both descriptions. The browser alone only places the x band in the right half. `N/type-matrix.test.ts:187–203`, `B/type-matrix.browser.test.ts:590–603,622–630` |\n| T-reference-donut | donut | Weak | The row excludes both lines and bands. Both citations supply a scalar y line. A donut that accepted a band would pass. `N/type-matrix.test.ts:242`, `B/type-matrix.browser.test.ts:636–643` |\n| T-limit-* | full | Established | Eight versus nine is tested directly. The donut tests also use eight positive slices plus zero and null, so they discriminate which entries count toward AX121. `N/type-matrix.test.ts:173–184`, `B/type-matrix.browser.test.ts:536–545,560–570`, `B/f8-donut.browser.test.ts:149–158` |\n| T-dense-donut | donut | Weak | For the thinnest slice, a path of the right colour starting at the expected angle passes even with zero angular extent. The model checks the length of the angles array. `B/type-matrix.browser.test.ts:443–460`, `N/f-dense.test.ts:213–218` |\n| F10 | area | Weak | Signed geometry, a positive stack total and a mixed-sign readout are covered. No readout assertion requires the sum of an all-negative stack. `N/f-stacks.test.ts:21–32,95–104`, `B/type-matrix.browser.test.ts:143–146,259–265` |\n| F10 | compact | Weak | Compact area and bar geometry are checked. Under the cell’s stated interpretation that the summary identifies the incomplete stack, a bare substring `incomplete` establishes neither which stack nor even an affirmative warning. `N/f-stacks.test.ts:72–94` |\n| A5 | donut | Weak | Background seams and both default palettes are measured. The seam test uses the light scheme alone, and the custom-background test makes the first colour exactly match the background. It does not discriminate the 3:1 threshold or show how to identify a named slice without colour. `B/a5-not-colour-alone.browser.test.ts:254–275,308–324` |\n| A8 | compact | Weak | All three compact kinds get axe scans. Loading, empty and error each pass the state precondition if *any* message is visible. The dirty case only has to show a figure, and fixtures are not crossed with states. `B/a6-a10.browser.test.ts:205–222,242–259` |\n| C5 | compact | Weak | All three kinds have an omission in the accessible description and painted ink in a corner. The marker’s own title can be any substring of the description. Even `See table.` reduces to an empty substring and passes. `B/compact.browser.test.ts:244–265` |\n| L6 | donut | Established | The title and subtitle appear inside the figure, and there are no axis titles. The axis and reference-label clauses do not apply to a donut. `B/l-legibility.browser.test.ts:557–579`, `N/reader-model.test.ts:366–370` |\n| DX10 | all six | Weak | The packed consumer compiles examples, and the dynamic tests actually render them and run per-example checks. The citation cannot credit those renders, and the workflow records that CI has never run. `apps/docs/test/examples.browser.test.ts:59–71,108–113,151–164`, `apps/docs/test/node.browser.test.ts:19–34`, `.github/workflows/ci.yml:1` |\n| P6 | all six | Not established for `d9fa4b0` | The record gives 99,347 bytes for line and 118,780 for everything, four bytes below the latter limit. It names a tarball digest. The checker neither matches that digest to this revision’s pack nor independently sources the budget. `bench/size-latest.json:4–30`, `acceptance/check.mjs:233–246,345–352` |\n\n## 2. Ten downgrades\n\n| Cell | Is the recorded gap real? | Does the remaining claim hold? |\n|---|---|---|\n| F8 donut | Yes. The grouped fixture contains zero and omits null. The browser fixture with null never triggers grouping. | Yes for the eight-positive threshold and the separate zero. Grouped null remains open. `N/f-donut.test.ts:91–111`, `B/f8-donut.browser.test.ts:149–158` |\n| F10 bar | Yes. The tooltip total is parsed for numbers, so dropping “incomplete” passes. | The table and keyboard value text do require “incomplete.” The all-negative readout also needs a gap. `N/f-stacks.test.ts:95–104` |\n| A1 compact | Partly. The browser scenarios for zone, `labelledBy` and 24-chart IDs use compact line. | “No test checks the time-zone statement” is too broad. A Node test checks the summary’s zone for **all three** compact kinds. Record the missing browser projection and cite the model test. `N/f-time.test.ts:61–74`, `B/a1-names.browser.test.ts:134–159` |\n| A2 line | Yes. Streaming traversal checks that the toolbar contains the word `Pause`. | Full-view roving focus is demonstrated. Reaching Pause, or the extra zoomed controls, by arrows remains open. `B/a2-keyboard.browser.test.ts:69–88,108–120` |\n| A8 area | Yes. Neither a pinned tooltip nor a small-plot strip is scanned. | Narrow the remaining state claim too. The three message states share the same visibility predicate, and the dirty case only checks for a figure. `B/a6-a10.browser.test.ts:205–222,249–259` |\n| A6 compact | Yes. The reflow/text-spacing loop explicitly selects full charts. | C3 supports ordinary compact sizing only. It never applies the spacing override to a compact state message. `B/a6-a10.browser.test.ts