s/docs/data/wcag.mjs:23,51,63–65`, `H/interaction.browser.test.ts:304–328`, `B/a4-table.browser.test.ts:152–162`\n\n## 5. The merge report’s findings\n\n| Test title | Finding |\n|---|---|\n| L7 “announced exactly once” | **Confirmed.** `announced()` converts the event list to a `Set` before the length check. Two identical announcements count as one. `B/l-legibility.browser.test.ts:634,675–677` |\n| I6 “tooltip … does not move” | **Confirmed.** The snapshot contains scene markup, description, value text and table. It has no tooltip field. `B/i1-pointer.browser.test.ts:1021–1032` |\n| T-zoom-scatter “+ narrows … visible y extremes change” | **Confirmed on both counts.** Scatter calls `zoom([12, 22])` directly, and the fixture retains the original 90–140 extrema. `B/type-matrix.browser.test.ts:275–287` |\n| C2 compact line “a null is a gap” | **Confirmed.** A segment bridging the gap can omit the vertex at x=2 and satisfy the assertion. The isolated-point assertion is independent. `B/compact.browser.test.ts:161–169` |\n| F8 “the ninth is what groups” | **Confirmed for this title.** Its fixture ends at eight. A different, cited T-limit test supplies the ninth and checks AX121, which is why T-limit-donut still earns an established verdict. `B/f8-donut.browser.test.ts:140–146`, `B/type-matrix.browser.test.ts:560–570` |\n\n| Checker or helper finding | Independent check |\n|---|---|\n| **1. Computed `it.each` under a suite prefix** | **Confirmed.** I ran the committed title scanner on the DX10 file. It returned the inventory-test title and `null` for the render suite. Runtime filenames cannot satisfy the expected null key. `acceptance/titles.mjs:193–216`, `acceptance/check.mjs:360–365,390–392` |\n| **4. Static registration accepts unreachable titles** | **Confirmed.** Given a `line, area` loop guarded by `type === \"line\"`, the committed scanner emitted both `only line` and `only area`. Its template matcher also accepted `only donut`. This affects structural validation. A real runtime pass still requires a matching result. `acceptance/titles.mjs:175–201,222–229`, `acceptance/check.mjs:114–123` |\n| **5. Size provenance** | **Confirmed.** The checker validates the record’s shape and uses its own `targetKiB`. I checked Git history: ten library source files changed between the commit last updating the record and `d9fa4b0`. The six P6 passes cannot be attributed to this tree. `acceptance/check.mjs:233–246,345–352`, `bench/size-latest.json:4–30` |\n| **8. Provenance errors still affect displayed statuses** | **Confirmed for the checker table.** Assertions enter the result index before provenance is judged. Release mode rejects the run through its exit code, but the table can display its passes. The docs consumer separately filters provenance. `acceptance/check.mjs:290,598–604,633–638`, `apps/docs/lib/conformance.mjs:124–126` |\n| **10. Motion signatures lose differences** | **Confirmed with a limit.** Equal-length signatures with the same last 120 characters compare equal after truncation. Returned frame-equality assertions can miss changes. `settledAt` is computed from full signatures first and is unaffected by that truncation. `B/checks.ts:172–177` |\n\nI ran the committed static checker against the commit snapshot, read-only. Its final counts were:\n\n```text\npass 6\nfail 0\nweak 151\nno evidence 0\nnot run 143\ncannot be verified here 11\nnot applicable 265\n```\n\nNo chart suite, browser suite, benchmark or manual rehearsal was run for this review. No files were edited and no contract change is needed.\n\n### Three fixes before release use\n\n1. **Make reported passes reproducible.** Bind P6 to the release-candidate pack and the spec budgets, exclude wrong-revision results from current cell statuses, and make DX10 enumerate its runtime examples. Then recompute the reachable count.\n2. **Put missing assertions in `gaps`.** Start with the ordinary paused view in I6, focused-stream changes in A7, F6 formatting in A4, and release-time